/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `kran_projects` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `kran_projects` VALUES (3,'Public Finance','Software for Finance Department','Y','N','Y','N','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Audit, Debt, Business Intelligence Dashboards','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Finance Department, Government of Jharkhand, plays a crucial role in ensuring the comprehensive development of the State. It is responsible for setting state priorities, efficiently managing resources from various sources, and overseeing the implementation of the Annual Plan. Established to enhance financial management and resource allocation, the department is pivotal in maintaining fiscal discipline and ensuring the State’s overall progress. Its Planning Division organizes resources based on state policies and requirements, while also focusing on institutional finance, non-budgetary resources, and the optimization of financial division gross resources.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The project is to build a cutting-edge Business Intelligence (BI) system, alongside a Debt Management module, Audit Management module, Mobile Apps/Platform, and an intuitive dashboard powered by BI Tools/Analytics Server. This solution aims to provide meaningful insights into fiscal data, allowing various departments to identify and address critical pain points, thus improving fiscal governance across the state. By leveraging the benefits of the implemented solution, the state can predict trends, identify growth opportunities, and recognize challenges in its fiscal performance.</p>','Finance Department','Govt of Jharkhand','project-modal.jpg','2024-11-04 12:35:47','A'),(4,'Public Finance','ESMAC','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Loan and HR Management System','\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Kerala state Co-operative Federation for Fisheries Development Ltd (Matsyafed), is an Apex Federation of primary level welfare societies in the coastal fishery sector. The objective of Matsyafed is ensuring the economic and social development of the fishermen community by implementing various schemes aimed at promoting the production, procurement, processing and marketing of fish and fish products. </p>','\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution automates the Loan & HR related activities of Matsyafed. The Loan Management module covers end to end functionalities right from Loan Application through its Processing, Sanction & Disbursement, Repayment, Recovery to its closure. It also covers Society Registration, One Time Settlement, Moratorium, Fund Management, and detailed MIS Reports. The Human Resource (HR) Management module maintains a digital service book with sub modules like Leave, Payroll, Transfer & Postings, Promotions, Performance Appraisal, Disciplinary Actions etc.</p>',' Fisheries Development Ltd (Matsyafed)','Kerala state Co-operative Federation','projects2.jpg','2024-11-04 13:03:55','A'),(5,'Public Finance','FinAssam','Y','Y','Y','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Integrated Finanacial Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. In order to improve efficiency and to bring in transparency in its functioning, the department was desirous of implementing a comprehensive Integrated Finance Management System for the state of Assam.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">FinAssam is the Financial Management Information System (FMIS) implemented for Government of Assam which consolidates all the financial information needs of the government into one information database. FinAssam comprises of a comprehensive suite of fully integrated software modules covering all the essential aspects of an effective Financial Management System. It is essentially a Single Source of Truth for the key decision makes of the state who are responsible for managing the financial resources.</p>','Finance Department','Govt of Assam','projects3.jpg','2024-11-04 12:30:42','A'),(6,'Public Finance','Sirius','Y','N','Y','N','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Macro Fiscal Aggregates & Projection','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Economics & Statistics is responsible for conducting economic surveys related to various aspects like agriculture, state income, market pricing, industrial statistics etc. The field level information is collected in various pre-defined forms. The Directorate is also responsible for maintaining the statistical data bank. It is proposed to put in place a software solution for the preparation of Macro Fiscal Projection for the Directorate of Economics & Statistics and the Directorate of Economic Affairs under the Finance Department, Government of Assam.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution facilitates software enabled preparation of Macro Fiscal Projection for the State of Assam. The implemented solution comprises of two key modules namely 1) Macro Fiscal Aggregates and 2) Macro Fiscal Projection. The solution manages collection, validation, consolidation of primary and secondary data from external sources for the projection & generation of macro fiscal projection. Sector wise forms are made available for the capture of survey data and in turn this data forms the basis for Macro Fiscal Projections.</p>','Directorate of Economic & Statistics','Govt. of Assam','projects4.jpg','2024-11-04 12:40:43','A'),(7,'Public Finance','AFC','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','Y','Y','N','N','N','Loan Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Assam Financial Corporation (AFC) is a statutory Corporation that was established as a Joint State Financial Corporation under Section 3(A) of the SFC’s Act 1951 way back in 1954 covering the erstwhile-undivided Assam with two union territories of Manipur and Tripura and operating in this North-East Region for more than five decades. As the premier Financial Institution (F.I.) in the North-East Region, it has a wide outreach at the grass root level compared to other Financial Institutions (FIs) and Banks. The main objective is to provide financial assistance to Micro, Small & Medium scale industries within its jurisdiction covering the North Eastern States of Assam, Meghalaya, Manipur and Tripura.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution caters to the automation needs of loan processing functions of the received applications. It manages the transactions related to loan repayments. Loan wise registers are maintained for easy reference. It also aids in the maintaining a comprehensive database of loan beneficiaries.</p>','Assam Financial Corporation','Govt of Assam','projects6.jpg','2024-11-04 13:01:20','A'),(8,'Public Finance','CharMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Charitable Endowments Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With a view to extend charity to the needy around us, Government of India formulated a set of rules, so as to enable the public to institute Charitable Endowments. As per the provisions contained in the Charitable Endowments Act of 1890, the Treasurer of Charitable Endowments, Kerala (The Director of Kerala State Audit Department) is empowered to govern the Endowments instituted in Kerala, as an agency of Government of Kerala.​ Endowment Funds are classified as General Fund and Amalgamated Fund.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The project primarily focuses on establishing a digital platform for managing all the Endowment related activities. The system has also got an automated Double Entry Accounting System, for recording all the Endowment related transactions. The solution covers the activities like Public Registration, Endowment Request, Endowment Request Processing / Approval, Initial Notification and Final Vesting Order, Endowment Creation and Management, FD Interest Management etc.</p>','Kerala State Audit Department','Govt. of Kerala','0.5096003515344593@-@projects6.jpg','2024-11-04 12:58:39','A'),(9,'Public Finance','LIMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Loan Information Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">National Safai Karamcharis Finance & Development Corporation (NSKFDC),    a wholly owned Govt. of India Undertaking under the Ministry of Social Justice & Empowerment (M/o SJ&E) was set up on  24th January 1997  as a Company “Not for Profit” under Section 25 of the Companies Act, 1956.  NSKFDC is in operation since October, 1997, as an Apex Corporation for the all-round socio-economic upliftment of the Safai Karamcharis, Scavengers and their dependants throughout India, through various loan and non-loan based schemes.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A comprehensive Loan Management System was implemented for NSKFDC. This solution covers the complete loan cycle right from the drawal submission by the SCAs / RRBs through its processing, disbursements, repayments to its closure. Quarterly demands are generated automatically and made available to SCA / RRB. All the associated SCAs & RRBs will have access to their relevant information over this online platform.</p>','National Safai Karmacharis','Finance & Development Corporation',NULL,'2024-11-04 12:45:23','A'),(10,'Public Finance','LEAP','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Loan and HR Software','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">National Backward Classes Finance & Development Corporation (NBCFDC) is a Govt of India Undertaking under the aegis of Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment. NBCFDC provides financial assistance through State Channelizing Agencies (SCAs) nominated by the respective State Governments/ UTs and Regional Rural Banks, Public Sector Banks. <br>\r\n    With growing challenges, NBCFDC has been aiming to achieve higher levels of efficiency in all its areas of operations. It is proposed to implement a web based Loan and HR Management System, to cater to ensure efficient utilization and management of resources.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The envisaged solution aids in automating Loan and HR management (LEAP – Loan & Employee information Automation Project) activities of the organization. It also facilitates maintenance of information pertaining to grants given to Training Institutes / Sector Skill Councils for promoting training programs on entrepreneurship development. Apart from NBCFDC users, SCAs, Banks, Sector Skill Councils and registered Training Institutes will have access to the system. A centralized digital system was put in place with access for the authorized users over the web.</p>','National Backward Classes','National Backward Classes',NULL,'2024-11-04 12:43:38','A'),(11,'Public Finance','AFEGU','Y','Y','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','Y','N','N','Financial Management Information System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Finance Department, Government of Assam had initiated various projects to automate the processes with regard to Monitoring Financial Information, Capturing Financial Transactions and Facilitating Integration with other Stake Holders of the Department like AG, RBI and Agency Banks dealing with the State Government. In this regard, various IT projects had already been initiated and are under different stages of implementation. In order to streamline the implementation of the ongoing projects, and to initiate newer projects within the Department, it is decided to setup an exclusive e-Governance unit within the Finance Department. It was proposed to procure external services from software firms for “IT Consulting and Technical Support Services” for the e-Governance unit.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">As part of the project, technical support & maintenance were provided to the various ongoing projects of the department. These projects include a) Integrated Government Financial Management Information System (IGFMIS) b) Macro Fiscal Projection (MFP) c) File Processing Solution at Directorate of Economics & Statistics and Directorate of Accounts and Treasuries d) Finance Department Computerization e) Digitization of Employee & Pensioner Database f) Software for the Directorate of Audit g) Establishing Connectivity up to the level of DDOs across the state.</p>','Finance Department',' Govt of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-04 12:49:38','A'),(12,'Public Finance','AIMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Audit Information Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Audit (Local Fund) is under the administrative control of the Finance Department. The Directorate conducts the audit of Local Fund Accounts in the state. It also conducts the audit of such other Non-Govt institutions and Govt. offices or any private institutions under the provisions of the certain Acts or Rules framed by the Govt. or under orders from the Government. Considering the large number of accounts to be audited every year involving a very large number of personnel across the state, the volume of routine and repetitive work in the department is very high.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Audit Information Management System “AIMS” is an end-to-end platform for managing the complete audit life cycle related to Local Self Government Institutions (LSGI). It covers the audit related activities right from the receipt of annual financial statements from LSGIs through audit calendar preparation, team formation, recording audit observations, generation of audit report and tracking it to closure. </p>','Directorate of Local Fund Audit','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-04 12:51:08','A'),(13,'Enterprise Resource Planning','SheSoft','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Custom Built ERP Class Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kerala State Women’s Development Corporation (KSWDC) was incorporated on 22nd February 1988 with the aim of expanding economic and social opportunities for the women of the State, especially those belonging to the marginalized and downtrodden sections of society. The prime objective of the Corporation is the empowerment of women by helping them overcome the constraints and challenges that hamper their growth and advancement. KSWDC seeks to bring women to the frontline of societal development. The helping hand of the Corporation has transformed the lives of many women and readied them to meet the challenges of life. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">SheSoft is a web-based solution that automates the core functional & administrative activities of KSWDC. The primary module is a fully Integrated Workflow enabled Loan Management System, primarily for NBFCs offering subsidized loans to specific target groups. The other areas covered as part of the project are Fund Management, Monitoring of Projects, Hostel Management, Training Management, Financial Accounting, HR Information, Court Cases, Assets & Intra Office Communication & Collaboration.</p>','Women\'s Development Corporation','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:38:37','A'),(14,'Public Finance','FIMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Financial Inspection Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Finance Inspection Wing was constituted in Finance Department in 1964 to ensure that financial rules and procedures are scrupulously followed by the departmental officers. The Inspection Party will conduct surprise inspection of Government Offices and report to Government cases of irregularity, slackness or indifference shown by Heads of Departments or Offices in the matter of financial control. The Inspection Party is empowered to scrutinize all files and registers relating to accounts, stores and other allied matters. They are also empowered to conduct physical verification of cash and stores wherever deemed necessary.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution covers the functionalities related with inspection management which includes the preparation and approval of inspection schedule, inspection report etc. It has the facility to prepare schedules of review meetings and to check the availability of participants. It includes file processing for correspondence other than inspection matters. In addition, a knowledge base is built in, which in turn acts as a reference tool for government orders, acts, rules and regulations. In brief it is an effective Inspection Monitoring System. A wide range of parameterized reports can be generated from the system.</p>','Finance Inspection Wing (Non-Technical)','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-04 12:53:20','A'),(15,'Public Finance','Probity FMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Financial Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Development of a system for financial planning and control has been recognised as one of the key components of the Institutional Strengthening Action Plan (ISAP) currently under implementation in the Public Works Department under Govt. of Kerala, ISAP is being implemented as part of the Kerala State Transport Project (KSTP) with the assistance of the World Bank. It was envisaged to implement a robust and comprehensive Financial Management System, riding over “Wings”, with thrust on greater integration of system with the core business of different wings and offices of PWD.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It is a financial accounting system which helps in the automation of major financial functions of the government project office based on single entry accounting system. It covers activities like budgeting, core accounting, resumption & reallocation, supplementary grants, surrender of funds, bills processing, receipts and payments etc. </p>','Transport Project','Kerala State',NULL,'2024-11-04 12:56:54','A'),(16,'Public Finance','Accounting Software','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Financial Accounting System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kerala Khadi and Village Industries Board (KVIB), is an organization set up by the Government of Kerala.  The primary focus of the organisation is in the development of small-scale industries and cottage industries amongst the traditional sector in the state. The organization assists the entrepreneurs to source, manufacture and sell their goods collectively. It also provides them with financial assistance and skill upgradation schemes. KVIB has offices, showrooms and warehouses in various parts of the state. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A software solution was developed and deployed at the Finance Department of the Board. The accounts of the 405 Production units and 140 Shops were maintained in the software. The software facilitates the finalization of accounts including the generation of Balance Sheet, Profit & Loss Statement and various other mandatory statements. The Loan Disbursement & Repayment Module maintains details of the beneficiaries of the loan scheme and their repayments. The software also keeps track of the production and sales of Khadi products in the various units of the organization.</p>','Kerala Khadi and Village Industries Board','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-04 13:05:06','A'),(17,'Public Finance','COSIS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Coir Co-operative Societies Information System (COSIS)','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Coir Development is a nodal agency set up by the Government of Kerala to facilitate the development of the Coir industry in the state. The Directorate has 10 project offices spread across the state, covering all the districts where the Coir industry has a major presence. Each project office has inspectors who oversee the functioning of a group of cooperative societies. There are about 700 cooperative societies in the state each having nearly 500 members. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Coir Co-operative Societies Information System (COSIS) maintains general information about societies, society staff and membership details. The loan module keeps track of the loans from disbursement to repayment. The process of registration & liquidation is taken care by the corresponding modules. Budget module tracks the Budget Provision under various Head of accounts allocated during the financial year. Employee module is a database of personnel in the Directorate and its Project Offices and is integrated with payroll.</p>','Directorate of Coir Development','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-04 13:07:25','A'),(18,'Public Finance','Loan Management System','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Margin Money Loan Management ','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Industries & Commerce is the Government department entrusted with the responsibility of providing all assistance to prospective entrepreneurs in the state. Apart from providing various information and other marketing / technology related assistance to the entrepreneurs, the directorate also provides help in the financing of the venture in the form of Margin money loans. These loans are sanctioned on various criteria and the interest rates are generally much lower than the regular financial institution rates. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The software solution was a workflow-based application facilitating the capture of information starting from receipt of application, routing of application to various officers, capturing the individual comments / notes, scrutinizing the documents submitted for processing, issuing correspondences to loan applicants and banks etc. The senior officers could monitor the progress of a loan application closely and if required view the notes written by various officers on the specific loan application. </p>','Directorate of Industries & Commerce','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-04 13:08:32','A'),(19,'Public Finance','Performance Monitoring System','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Performance Monitoring of PSUs','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Restructuring and Internal Audit Board (RIAB) is responsible for the monitoring of performance of the public sector undertakings of the Govt. of Kerala. Based on orders received and the value of orders, RIAB releases working capital funding to the PSUs. RIAB monitors the utilization of the amount released towards the working capital by the respective PSU. The solution involved the setting up of a reporting mechanism between the PSUs and RIAB. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The software facilitates the filling up of all the relevant information by each PSU and the same is updated on the server at RIAB. Depending on various factors like the PSU, the category of the information etc., the software will route the information to the concerned financial analyst in RIAB who in turn process the information and puts it up to higher authorities for approval. Once approved the concerned PSU will get the information of the approval details. Facility is provided to generate various reports from the software covering performance of individual PSUs, total requests for funding handled by RIAB during a period, requests denied, etc.</p>','Restructuring and Internal Audit Board (RIAB)','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-04 13:10:01','A'),(20,'Permits, Licensing & Compliance','Nirman Shramik','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Workers Welfare Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Odisha Building & Other Construction Workers’ Welfare Board has been constituted to extend different types of social security and other welfare benefits under Nirman Shramik Kalyana Yojana (NSKY). Cess @ 1% of the cost of construction incurred by an employer/ builder is being collected with effect from 15.12.2008 and being deposited in the fund of Odisha Building & Other Construction Workers’ Welfare Board for welfare of the building workers. The Board extends the benefits to registered Building & Other Construction Workers under NSKY: Assistance in case of accident, Death Benefit, Assistance for funeral expenses, Medical Assistance etc.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It is a web enabled solution for managing the key activities of OBCWWB like Registration, Cess Collection, and Disbursement of Welfare Benefits etc. The solution automates the key activities of Odisha Building & Other Construction Workers’ Welfare Board. It also aids in proper management of corpus funds. The Dashboard and MIS reports facilitate the organization to monitor their day-to-day activities in an efficient manner. The solution facilitates timely processing and disbursement of benefits to the registered workers. </p>','Odisha Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Fund Board','Govt. of Odisha',NULL,'2024-11-05 12:40:25','A'),(21,'Permits, Licensing & Compliance','Phoenix','Y','N','Y','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Unified Digital Platform for the Board','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kerala State Pollution Control Board is established as a regulatory authority for implementing various pollution control laws. The Board is charged with enforcing laws related to environmental protection and has undertaken various studies of underground water, solid and air to take remedial steps to control pollution. The Board is committed to provide pollution free environment to the people of the State. The Core activities includes Water and Air Pollution Control, Waste Management, Legal Actions, Laboratory Investigations, Public awareness etc.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It is a centralized digital platform that helps to manage and monitor the implementation of various Acts and Rules set by the State Pollution Control Board. The solution aids in automating the key functional and administrative areas of the Board which includes Consent Management, Waste & Returns Management, Laboratory Management, Complaint Management, Legal Actions Management, and Collaboration Suite. The solution provides a comprehensive profiling of all registered industries / establishments.</p>','Kerala State Pollution Control Board','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 12:41:46','A'),(22,'Permits, Licensing & Compliance','PAReSHRAM','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Digital Platform for Delivery of various Services','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Department of Labour and ESI, is dedicated to ensuring compliance with labour laws and regulations. It is mandated with the key functions like Labour Welfare and Administration of Labour Laws, Inspection of Safety measures of Factories & Boilers and Administration of Factories & Boilers Acts & Rules, Social Security Schemes for Industrial Workers, like E.S.I (Employee State Insurance), Employment and Vocational Guidance to the Youth, Adjudication of Industrial Disputes, and Child Labour Welfare.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">PAReSHRAM is the web portal of the Labour & ESI Department of the Government of Odisha. As a Digital Platform, it offers quick digital access to all the services delivered by both, the Directorate of Labour & the Directorate of Factories & Boilers, under various Labour & Factory Acts. This platform streamlines and automates 67 services offered by the Labour & ESI Department. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">PAReSHRAM ensures a fully paperless processing system, as all application submissions, processing, and approval/rejection procedures occur entirely online. Final certificates are exclusively issued with digital signatures, ensuring authenticity and security. Moreover, all output reports feature a QR code, allowing other organizations to verify the legitimacy of certificates issued by the Department.</p>','Labour & ESI Department','Govt. of Odisha',NULL,'2024-11-05 12:42:57','A'),(23,'Permits, Licensing & Compliance','HFIS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Hazardous Factory Information System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Factories & Boilers is the statutory authority of the State Government for implementing rules and regulations regarding safety in the industries sector. The Directorate has the role of closely monitoring the safety mechanisms in the various factories. Regular inspections are held by the Directorate personnel to ensure the conformity of mandatory systems and procedures in the factories. Considering the large number of factories in the state, keeping track of the inspections and the details of each factory had become very difficult. It was therefore decided to put in place a software solution to keep track of the same.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution maintains the information pertaining to factories of hazardous nature. It forms a central repository and all relevant information can be updated from time to time. The solution was based on client server architecture. It maintains the information of all chemicals used for production. The usage ratings of each chemical will be also mentioned. Alerts will be generated on exhaustive use of chemicals that can lead to unwarranted situations. Also, a wide range of customised reports can be generated on demand.</p>','Directorate of Factories & Boilers','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 12:43:58','A'),(24,'Permits, Licensing & Compliance','FABOS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Factories and Boilers Online System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Factories & Boilers is the statutory authority for implementing statutes meant to improve the Safety, Welfare and Health of factory personnel in the State. The department was involved in the activities primarily related with issue & renewal of licenses to factories. It is a tedious task for the inspectors to manually keep track of the licensing procedures. The priority was to build up databases for all activities related to factories & boilers in the state.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The software consists of four modules namely Factory Information System (FIS), Boiler Information System (BIS) & Factory License Renewal System (FLRS). FIS is a database of all the factories across the state, which forms the primary data for the automated system. BIS is a database of boilers and FLRS takes care of the processing of factory license issue & renewal.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"> Once the database is in place then it would be easy to automate the functions of license issue & renewal. All the modules were developed as standalone applications. The master data could be captured into these databases that could be later utilized for networked version.</p>','Directorate of Factories and Boilers','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 12:44:58','A'),(25,'Permits, Licensing & Compliance','BIS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Boiler Information System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Factories & Boilers is the statutory authority for implementing statutes meant to improve the Safety, Welfare and Health of factory personnel in the State. The department was involved in the activities primarily related with issue & renewal of licenses to factories. It is a tedious task for the inspectors to manually keep track of the licensing procedures. The priority was to build up databases for all activities related to factories & boilers in the state.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Solution is an end-to-end system for availing services provided by Directorate of Factories and Boilers to the Boiler owners, which helps in efficient and faster processing of requests. This includes submission of applications, renewal of various services, online payment facility, SMS Integration etc.</p>','Directorate of Factories and Boilers',' Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 12:45:52','A'),(26,'General Administration','STAGE','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','File Management, Repository of Acts, Rules, Regulations','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Accounts and Treasuries, Assam is a head of department under Finance Department of Government of Assam as declared by Government and listed in the Schedule IV of the Delegation of Financial Power Rules of Government of Assam. The Directorate is headed by Director from the Assam Finance Service (AFS) cadre and he is assisted by a group of AFS officers. The key function is that of administering day to day treasury business of the state government.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Speedy and Transparent Administration in Government Establishments “STAGE” is a first step towards paperless office in the organization. The key features of the solution include registration & routing of inward correspondence, file creation, processing & routing, file linking, file closing & archiving, file tracking information, file take over facility, remote access over internet, remote document submission, knowledgebase, exhaustive search, stock file / stock tray, call book, reminder diary, notings, drafts, instant messaging. Various parameterized reports can be generated on demand.</p>','Directorate of Accounts & Treasury','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:23:50','A'),(27,'General Administration','eAdmin','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Registration cum Membership of Exporters & other Admin areas','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Federation of Indian Export Organizations (FIEO) was set up jointly by the Ministry of Commerce, Government of India and private trade and industry for in promoting India’s exports. As FIEO’s interests and objectives cover the entire gamut of India’s international trade with special focus on exports, its activities and programmes are multiple and directed towards assisting its members to extend their global reach and increase their exports. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">As an apex body, it constantly thrives to improve and upgrade the export policy and the associated administrative, financial and operational machinery of the Central and State Governments, as well as the infrastructural and fiscal support available to exporters.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The objective of the project was to develop a suite of applications to automate the core administrative as well as functional areas of the organization. The solution includes functional modules for Registration cum Membership of Exporters, Trade & Tender Enquiries and Exporter’s Problem Management System. It also covers administrative modules for HR, File Processing & Tracking Solution and Intranet Software. </p>','Federation of Indian Export Organizations','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:25:55','A'),(28,'General Administration','eAdmin','N','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Human Resource Management System',NULL,'f','Terumo Penpol','',NULL,'2024-07-30 18:17:16','A'),(29,'General Administration','eAdmin','N','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Administrative ERP Solution',NULL,'f','NORKA - ROOTS','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-07-30 18:17:56','A'),(30,'General Administration','STAGE','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Electronic File Management','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Ministry of Finance, Govt. of India has under its wings four major departments viz. Dept. of Economic Affairs, Dept. of Expenditure, Dept. of Revenue and Dept. of Disinvestments. Each of these departments receives and processes a very large number of correspondences every day. Some of the received correspondences are converted to New Files and others are filed in Existing Files. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With the very high number of files being handled, it is extremely difficult to locate a file as and when needed. Considering the confidential nature of the files being handled, it is also required to identify all those who have handled the file at each stage. To keep track of the status of these files / correspondences and to retrieve the same at short notice is virtually impossible in most government offices. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Considering the nature and the importance of the files that are processed in the Ministry, it was recommended to put in place an RFID enabled solution, which would keep track of the physical files within the office premises. The solution will have the facility for inward registration, acknowledgement generation, routing of correspondence, new file creation, make notings, prepare draft correspondence, issue approved correspondence, and maintain despatch register.</p>','Ministry of Finance','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:28:11','A'),(31,'General Administration','eAdmin','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Cadre Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Controller General of Accounts, Govt. of India is responsible for the compilation of the Union Government’s Accounts. The Annual Accounts of the Union Government comprising the Union Finance and Appropriation Accounts, are laid before Parliament along with the Audit report thereon. The Office of the Controller General of Accounts (CAG), employs around 10,000 personnel in 4 categories viz. Group A, B, C & D. These personnel are deployed in various ministries and in various states across the country.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All administration processes with regard to human resources are managed through manual processes. In order to effectively utilize this large resource of manpower trained in various specific areas, it is required to implement a well-designed and structured Cadre Management System. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The proposed solution eAdmin aims to re-create the existing manual system in a government office without effecting any major modifications. The software is web-enabled and can take care of Employee Information, Promotion Processing, Deputation Processing, Transfer Processing, Court Case Monitoring, Disciplinary action monitoring and Training Management. </p>','Controller General of Accounts','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:29:24','A'),(32,'General Administration','STAGE','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Electronic File Management','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kerala State Electricity Board (KSEB) is the sole agency responsible for Generation and Distribution of electrical power in the state. KSEB is a Government of Kerala owned establishment. At the Head office of the organization, there are over 25 various departments each headed by a senior officer. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Heads of Departments report to the Board Secretariat through the Board Secretary. The number of files/correspondences received and processed in the Board Secretariat is very high and each file/correspondence is important and confidential. It is often difficult to find a particular file/correspondence that is submitted to the Board Secretariat from the department. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A software solution for File Management was developed and implemented at the Board Secretariat to keep track of the files/correspondences received. The solution keeps track of files/correspondences received, to whom forwarded for action, instructions, officer and date. Responses or reply could also be kept in the system. The File Management System would be able to record and retrieve the movement / location of each file, note and mail within Secretariat. Decisions on important files can be accessed only with specific authentication. </p>','Kerala State Electricity Board','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:31:02','A'),(33,'General Administration','Office Automation','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Functional & Administrative Automation','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Industries & Commerce is the Govt. department entrusted with the responsibility of providing all assistance to prospective entrepreneurs in the state. Apart from providing all necessary information to the public, the department also assists in the form of providing constructed building space on lease, developed plots, common research facilities, machinery leasing etc. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The department helps in financing the ventures of eligible applicants as well. The department has over half a dozen major functional requirements that were currently being done by manual methods. Also, as the department had offices across the state the compilation of information was becoming increasingly difficult.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A total solution encompassing all the functional requirements of the organisation was the immediate requirement. Automation was necessary to a large extent to reduce the drudgery of the employees and also to compile complicated and voluminous reports from across the state. A software solution was designed, developed and implemented covering the following areas like Small Scale Industries Registration, Women Industrial Programme Management, Co-operative Society Database, State Investment Subsidy Management, Budget Monitoring, and PMRY Loan Management</p>','Directorate of Industries & Commerce','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:32:24','A'),(34,'Direct Benefit Transfer','Software for Science & Technology Council','Y','N','Y','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Scheme Management','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Science & Technology Department plays a vital role in the development and promotion of science & technology for the welfare of the people in the State. The Department implements several schemes and programs for promoting and popularizing science and technology. These Schemes and Programs are implemented with clear and transparent guidelines, terms & conditions, and with strict norms to ensure full accountability and uphold quality of education and research.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each scheme follows a unique management model by which an Expert External Committee reviews the proposals, screen out low-quality proposals and select the best projects, and also recommends the quantum of research fund, conduct thorough review periodically for monitoring the progress of the projects.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution is a Web Portal along with Online Services for State Council on Science & Technology Department, for achieving excellence in basic research, promoting academia-industry interactions, strengthening indigenous initiatives, and building strong infrastructure, in addition to facilitating and developing a high-quality science education system in the State.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">This e-Governance Solution facilitates the registration of beneficiaries such as Individual / Institution / Organization for various Schemes / Programs, Benefit Management with request processing, transfer of benefits through IFMS, Mobile Application for Registration, Inspection and Query Management. Dashboard and MIS report generate valuable and timely reports such as Beneficiary Master, Schemes, Benefits Given, and Defaulters List etc. that facilitate better control of the Dept. affairs and enhance the efficiency of day-to-day operations.</p>','Counil on Science & Technology','Govt. of Odisha',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:19:25','A'),(35,'Direct Benefit Transfer','HPC Grant','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Direct Benefit Transfer','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. Considering the need to address the financial assistance required by the the children of the employees of Nagon & Cacher Paper Mills under Hindustan Paper Corporation Mills in Assam, the department devised a scheme named HPC Grant.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">HPC Grant is a one-time special education Grant Initiated by the Government of Assam.<br>\r\nIt aims to promote education and help support academic pursuits for the children of the employees of Nagon & Cacher Paper Mills under Hindustan Paper Corporation Mills in Assam. The grant amount shall be awarded to eligible candidates as per the set norms of the scheme. The solution is a DBT portal that facilitates easy processing and disbursement of benefits directly to the beneficiaries.</p>','Finance Department','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:20:37','A'),(36,'Direct Benefit Transfer','Financial Outreach Program (Migrant Assist)','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Direct Benefit Transfer','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. Considering the need to provide immediate financial assistance to the migrant workers who got held up during the covid related national lockdown, the department devised a scheme to quickly reach out to the workers and provide immediate relief to them. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">This DBT project was aimed to address the immediate financial needs of more than 1 million migrant workers stranded outside the State of Assam affected due to the nationwide lockdown. The Government of Assam took a quick and well-planned decision and put up a project immediately whereby the stranded persons could reach out to the government by means of a web portal.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A dedicated helpline was established for reaching out to the beneficiaries. This is one among the 5 major flagship IT projects successfully carried out by KRAN under the Assam CARES initiative started by the Government of Assam. Fastest Development and Implementation - The project was Conceptualized, Designed, and rolled out in a record time of 48 hours.</p>','Finance Department','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:21:43','A'),(37,'Direct Benefit Transfer','Orunodoi','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Direct Benefit Transfer','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Orunodoi is the biggest DBT scheme initiated by the Government of Assam till date. It aims to provide relief to families when it comes to food and nutritional security and concentrate on education and health of their families. Women being the primary caretaker of a family, are kept as the primary beneficiary for this scheme. Every eligible household will receive a benefit of INR 830.00 per month. DBT to the bank account of the nominated female member of the family.</p>','Finance Department','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:22:38','A'),(38,'Direct Benefit Transfer','Re-Svayem','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N',NULL,'N','Direct Benefit Transfer','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. The government has initiated a scheme to provide financial assistance to the entrepreneurs and encourage an industry friendly environment in the state.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Svayem is a DBT scheme initiated by the Government of Assam to promote an entrepreneurship-oriented ecosystem. It aims to form youth groups on the line of SHGs (Self-Help Groups) and provide to them with seed capital to initiate entrepreneurial activities and linking them for credit extension to banks/ financial institutions. The money can be used for setting up enterprising new activities or expanding existing business. For every eligible Self-Help Groups (SHGs), Joint Liability Groups (JLGs), Farmer Producer Organizations (FPO), Cluster-Level SPVs/ Federations of the State, each member will receive a benefit of INR 50,000 DBT to the bank account of the selected SHG/ JLG/ FPOs/SPVs.</p>','Finance Department','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:23:45','A'),(39,'Direct Benefit Transfer','Abhinandan','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Direct Benefit Transfer','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. In order to provide a relief to the students who has already availed educational loans, the department has devised a scheme to waive off the existing loans. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Abhinandan is an Educational Loan Subsidy Scheme initiated by the Government of Assam. It aims to provide loan waiver to students of Assam who have availed education loans. This will help all those who are not able to pursue higher education due to insufficient funds. In this scheme, around 50,000 subsidies will be provided on educational loans to all the students who want to pursue higher studies. It will provide a one-time subsidy of Rs. 50,000, which will be deposited in the loan account as DBT to the bank account of the beneficiary.</p>','Finance Department','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:25:56','A'),(40,'Direct Benefit Transfer','Aponar Apon Ghar','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Direct Benefit Transfer','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. Considering the need of homeless families of the state, the department has launched a scheme to provide housing loans to eligible applicants for facilitating the construction of own home.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Aponar Apon Ghar is a DBT scheme initiated by the Government of Assam, wherein, all applicants get home loans at subsidized interest rates. It aims to provide financial relief to the people of Assam and to ease the access to housing loans for the purchase or construction of the first house for the family. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The housing loan can be availed from any Scheduled Commercial Bank, Regional Rural Bank, Assam Cooperative Apex Bank within the State. Every permanent resident of Assam will be eligible to avail the scheme. Government as well as private employees and even journalists can apply and avail benefits of the scheme. It will provide all citizens a subsidy of up to Rs 2.5 lakhs on home loans from 5 lakhs up till Rs 40 lakhs as DBT to the bank account of the applicant. </p>','Finance Department','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:27:26','A'),(41,'Enterprise Resource Planning','RISe','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Y','Custom Built ERP Class Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Santacruz Electronic Export Processing Zone was established as a specialized EPZ solely for the production and export of electronic goods, covering an area of 110 acres leased from the Maharashtra Industrial Development Corporation (MIDC) in Andheri (East). Considering the high potential and the pollution-free nature of Gem & Jewellery Industry, the Govt. of India decided to permit manufacture and export of Gem & Jewellery items from SEEPZ. SEEPZ was one of the three export processing zones converted into a special economic zone in 1st November 2000. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution automates the key functional, administrative, financial, and managerial areas of SEEPZ SEZ. This solution helps to assist in monitoring and reviewing of all activities of SEEPZ SEZ and optimize its operations, improve efficiency and communication resulting in reduced costs. It is a complete, modular, and customizable solution that can be adapted to any business size or type. The major areas covered include estate management, financial accounting, routine & general administration activities and GIS.</p>','SEEPZ SEZ','Mumbai',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:37:18','A'),(42,'Enterprise Resource Planning','SmartOffice','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Administrative ERP Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Commissionerate of Police (CoP)– Kochi City, Kerala State, has on its rolls over 3000 Police Personnel at various levels and a vehicle fleet numbering over 250. The CoP has nearly 20 sub offices and a central administrative office manned by around 60 administrative staff. All administrative activities of CoP – Kochi City were managed through manual systems. This includes Personnel Administration, Financial Administration, Fleet Administration etc. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A detailed study was conducted at the Commissionerate of Police – Kochi City to identify the routine and repetitive tasks carried out by the administrative sections in the office. Based on the study, 20 areas amenable to computerisation were identified. SmartOffice, a suite of software applications, was developed specifically catering to each of the identified areas. SmartOffice comprises of 20 Software modules that are interdependent and fully integrated. </p>','Commissionerate of Police','Thiruvananthapuram, Kochi, Kozhikode',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:39:54','A'),(43,'Enterprise Resource Planning','SmartOffice','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Administrative ERP Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The State Police Headquarters of Kerala has the overall administrative responsibility of the entire police establishment in the state. The Kerala PHQ has over 500 sub offices and a central administrative office manned by around 200 administrative staff. All administrative activities of Kerala PHQ were managed through manual systems. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Because of the unique nature of the department, it is often necessary to generate accurate reports within a very short time frame. Due to the very high volume of work, this is not always possible and leads to delay in decision-making. As the decision at the PHQ has a cascading effect down to the district offices, this has an adverse impact on the overall efficiency of the department.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A detailed study conducted at the Kerala State Police Headquarters identified 20 areas amenable for computerisation in the administrative sections of the office. The study at the PHQ was done based on the earlier study conducted at the District Office of the department (CoP – Kochi).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"> SmartOffice, a suite of software applications was developed specifically catering to each of the identified areas. SmartOffice comprises of 20 Software modules that are interdependent and fully integrated. SmartOffice for PHQ also envisages the requirement of integrating and consolidation of information from the various district offices of the department. </p>','Police Headquarters','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:41:29','A'),(44,'Others','SmartCampus','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','School Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Love Dale Residential School, a new-age educational institution located in Attingal, Trivandrum, is taking a significant step towards automation by developing a comprehensive software application to manage its operations. Committed to achieving higher efficiency across all areas, the school is actively streamlining its activities to better serve its community. While the current systems were once sufficient, they can no longer meet the evolving day-to-day needs of the institution. By digitizing essential aspects of school management, Love Dale aims to foster meaningful changes that will enhance its educational environment. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">SmartCampus is an Enterprise class solution that automates the key activities of Love Dale Residential School such as Academic, Administrative, Human Resources and Financial areas. It maintains a comprehensive student profile right from the admission process through various curricular & extra-curricular activities to the point of leaving the school. Routine administrative tasks are also handled through this platform. Parents can have a view of the academic details of their wards at their fingertips.</p>','Love Dale Residential School','Attingal',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:29:32','A'),(45,'Others','Track & Trace (Quarantine Management for Covid-19)','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','Y','N','Track & Trace','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. During the testing times of Covid, the government was quick enough to put in place a mechanism to track and trace the quarantine procedures laid out by the state.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Based on the data collected from Financial Outreach Program, the Government of Assam was able to plan for the huge numbers of stranded residents who would be returning to their homes. They took quick and effective decision to set up an end to end tracking and management system related to all the quarantine procedures mandated by the State. An online platform to track, screen, monitor and manage the quarantine procedures for residents entering the State.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It maintains detailed records of Screened Applicants, Samples Collected, Number of Quarantined Individuals and details of further testing (both migrants and natives) Each sample collected is linked to a unique SRF number provided during RT-PCR test. The portal was Conceptualized, Designed, and rolled out in a record time of 48 hours.</p>','Quarantine Management','Govt. of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:31:08','A'),(46,'Others','AdMIRe','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Advertisement Management Information Repository','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Public Relations (DPR) primarily handles the task of dissemination of information about the various Government Programs and compiles news items pertaining to public feedback from the Print and Electronic Media. Other responsibilities of the department includes conducting various awareness and mass contact programs on behalf of the State Government, issuing accreditation to Journalists, providing retirement benefits to journalists, issue of various tender advertisements on behalf of Government and Public Sector Undertakings. The Directorate has 3 Regional Offices and 14 District Offices located across the state. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">AdMIRe is a comprehensive online system for I&PRD that aids in the automation of its core functional activities. Once implemented, it helps in administering the department as a compact entity enhancing operational efficiency to a large extent. The software comprises of functional modules like Press Clipping Management, Journalist Pension, Release Order Management and administrative modules like File Processing and Tracking Solution and Intranet.</p>','Information & Public Relations Department','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:40:38','A'),(47,'Others','BMEDS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Drug Distribution & Equipment Maintenance System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Bihar Medical Services & Infrastructure Corporation Limited (BMSICL) is set up by the Govt. of Bihar Medical Services & Infrastructure Corporation (BMSIC) under the aegis of the Department of Health and Family Welfare (DoHFW). Bihar Medical Services & Infrastructure Corporation Limited (BMSICL) is incorporated on 26th July 2010 under section 617 of Indian Company Act 1956 as per the Sankalp cum Memo no. 466(12) Dated 19.05.2010 of Health Department, Government of Bihar and is responsible for the procurement of quality drugs, equipments, services and works for the DoHFW. One of the key objectives of BMSICL is to act as the central procurement agency for all essential drugs and equipments for all public healthcare institutions (hereinafter referred to as user institutions) under the department.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">“BMEDS” – Bihar Medical Equipments and Drugs System for BMSICL is a Web Based Software Solution for automation of the two main functional activities of BMSICL covering Drug Projection / Procurement / Distribution / Payment Processing/ Stock Monitoring and Equipment Procurement / Installation /Service Monitoring / Payment Monitoring. The stake holders of the project includes End User Institutions under DHS / DME, Authorized officers at DHS and DME, Vendors and Testing Labs apart from officials of BMSICL.</p>','Bihar Medical Services & Infrastructure Development Corporation','Govt. of Bihar',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:43:54','A'),(48,'Enterprise Resource Planning','TASK','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Total Automation System for KMSCL','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kerala Medical Services Corporation Limited (KMSCL) is a fully owned Government of Kerala company set up in 2007 for providing services to various health care institutions under Department of Family Welfare and Health. One of the key objectives of the KMSCL is to act as the central procurement agency for all essential drugs and equipments for all public healthcare institutions (hereinafter referred to as user institutions) under the department. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The company is procuring drugs worth more than Rs.170 Crores & above 250 different types of medical equipments and also provides essential services needed for health sector. It has also been mandated with the setting up and running of all kinds of modem Medical and Paramedical or medical based ancillary facilities such as hospitals, pathological labs, diagnostic centers, x-ray/scanning facilities. The Government of Kerala formulated KMSCL. It is proposed to implement a comprehensive solution covering the core functional as well as administrative areas of the organization. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">“TASK” – Total Automation Solution for KMSCL is a web based solution built on open technologies that caters to the total automation needs of the organization. The solution is work flow enabled wherein users will have different roles and responsibilities. The key areas covered are drug procurement, quality check and its distribution, equipment procurement, allocation and its maintenance, HR management, file management, asset management, financial accounting.</p>','Medical Services Corporation Ltd','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:43:43','A'),(49,'Others','UTRN','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Universal Trial Reference Number','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The World Health Organization (WHO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations dedicated to promoting global health and well-being. Established in 1948 and headquartered in Geneva, Switzerland, WHO works to ensure health for all by setting international health standards, conducting research, and providing support to countries in various health domains. In November 2004, during the Ministerial Summit on Health Research, a call to action was made for stakeholders to establish a platform linking international clinical trials registers, as outlined in the Mexico Statement on Health Research.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The need is to generate a unique Universal Trial Reference Number for each of the clinical trials submitted to the International Clinical Trials Registry Platform’s Search Portal. This number aids as an easy reference tool to search a particular trial on a later date. A significant outcome of this project is the Universal Trial Reference Number (UTRN), designed to facilitate the unique identification of clinical trials submitted to the International Clinical Trials Registry Platform\'s (ICTRP) Search Portal.</p>','World Health Organization','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:45:16','A'),(50,'Others','Inmate Management System','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Inmate management system ','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Prison Headquarters is situated at Thiruvananthapuram and is headed by the Director General of Police, Prisons. An Ex-Cadre post of I.G.P (prisons) has been created to assist the DGP. The Head of the Department is assisted by the Southern Deputy Inspectors General. There are three Regional Offices, one in Kozhikode headed by Deputy Inspector General of Prisons who supervises the Northern Region and another in Thrissur to supervise the Central Region and the third in Thiruvananthapuram. There are 3 Central jails, 3 District Jails, 5 special jails, 28 sub jails, 2 open jails 1 women’s prison and one borstal school.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">This software maintains the details of prisoners or inmates of prisons across different prisons of the state. The details maintained include general, identification, bail, appeal, parole, remission, warrant, medical history, wages and release. Once registered, a unique number is generated for each prisoner and it helps in the easy identification if the same person revisits. It facilitates the DGP / IG to have information at their fingertips for efficient monitoring of prisoner information.</p>','Department of Prisons','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:46:33','A'),(51,'Enterprise Resource Planning','Saarathi','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Total Automation System for KSRTC','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kerala Road Transport Corporation (K S R T C) was established by the Government of Kerala in 1965. K S R T C is the only public transport system that caters to the road transport needs of the people of the state. The corporation has a fleet strength of 4704 Nos. comprising of 2940 Leyland, 1562 Tata, 200 Eicher and 2 Volvos. Out of these 2124 buses (45.15%) are aged more than 7 years of life. Apart from the state wide service inter-state buses are also operated by the Corporation. In order to leverage the benefits of information technology the Corporation aims at automating the key functional as well as administrative areas.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution was a suite of over 50 interdependent applications to automate the core administrative as well as functional areas of the organization so that the organization can be effectively managed as a compact entity. The major software applications suites are for Fleet Management, Revenue Management, Schedule Management and various other administrative functions. Also covered are Financial Accounting and corporate Intranet solution. Routine reports would be generated automatically from the respective software modules. </p>','Kerala State Road Transport Corporation','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:44:58','A'),(52,'Others','Indenture','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Order and Payment Processing Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">KPHCC specializes in civil construction and maintenance, serving the Kerala Police Department and the Kerala Government. Headquartered in Trivandrum, the corporation manages projects across the state through a dedicated team of project engineers. To execute its diverse projects, KPHCC collaborates with specialized subcontractors, inviting tenders for specific tasks based on approved designs and schedules. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Work orders are issued to qualified contractors offering competitive quotes. Recognizing the inefficiencies of manual order and payment processing, KPHCC decided to automate and streamline work order generation and payment workflows, significantly reducing processing time and enhancing operational efficiency.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution aids in the automation of the major functional activities of the Police Housing Construction Corporation right from the acceptance of a project through the preparation of drawings and schedules, tendering, monitoring and effecting payments. The software application consists of various modules like Processing of Orders, E-Tendering (Comprise sub modules like Vendor Registration, Tender Notification, Bid Submission, Bid Comparison & Vendor History), Issuing Work Orders, Progress Monitoring, M-Book Management (M-Book Preparation & M-Book Verification), Bill Preparation & Bill Processing. Once deployed the solution aids in streamlining the work order generation and payment processing activities of the organization.</p>','Kerala Police Housing and Construction Corporation Ltd','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:47:45','A'),(53,'General Administration','SmartWings','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','File Management and Intranet','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">No. 5 Wing is a vital unit of the Indian Air Force (IAF) located at Kalaikunda Air Force Station in West Bengal. Established to support various air operations, the wing plays a crucial role in the training and operational readiness of IAF personnel. The wing provides essential training, maintenance, and operational support for aircraft, engaging in missions that include combat readiness, tactical operations, and joint exercises with other branches of the armed forces. Equipped with modern aircraft and facilities, No. 5 Wing ensures high standards of operational effectiveness and readiness.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The No.5 Wing, Kalaikunda was keen on implementing a computerised solution for automating the entire file movement of the wing. It also needed a solution for effective communication between users within the organisation. SmartWings is a software solution for office automation designed and developed to suit the requirements of a typical office.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It has been customised to suit the exact needs of No. 5 Wing, Kalaikunda. It consists of two unique software products STAGE and INTRANET. While STAGE addresses the requirements of File Processing, INTRANET provides for the intra office communication between the users.</p>','No 5 Wing','Indian Air Force, Kalaikunda',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:16:26','A'),(54,'Public Finance','ProMIS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Project Monitoring Information System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. In order to strengthen the monitoring of the ongoing projects undertaken by the government, the department decided to put in place a centralized digital project monitoring tool.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">ProMIS is a project monitoring tool that aids in maintaining the details of all the projects undertaken by the government. It maintains details like General details, Cost details, Funding details, Funds received, Funds released to executing Agencies, Schedules & Milestones tracking, Physical progress tracking etc. Based on these details captured, various dashboards and reports are generated. The dashboard displays alerts on milestones, reviews, etc. Various graphical charts are provided which help in analyzing the current project position.</p>','Finance Department','Govt of Assam',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:14:49','A'),(55,'Public Finance','Accounting System','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','National Health Accounts System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (MOHFW) is a vital government body in India dedicated to enhancing public health and family welfare through effective policy formulation and implementation. In 2003, the MOHFW established the National Health Account (NHA) Cell in collaboration with the World Health Organization (WHO) to promote transparency and efficiency in healthcare financing.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">This initiative aims to provide comprehensive data on health expenditures, helping to inform policy decisions and improve resource allocation. Through innovative solutions and partnerships, the Ministry strives to foster a healthier nation for all citizens.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">National Health Accounts (NHA) is responsible for tracking the Health Resource utilization, analyzing health fund distribution across different services, tracking health expenditure trends and making financial projection of national health system requirements. The software solution enables the NHA Cell to generate various reports in short notice.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The financial data can to be presented in various formats for analytical and decision-making purposes. The software facilitates multiple personnel of the NHA to access and update information simultaneously and also permit others with authorisation to generate various reports on demand. </p>','Ministry of Health and Family Welfare','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:13:40','A'),(56,'Others','CTRI','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Clinical Trials Registry of India','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Clinical Trials Registry - India (CTRI) is a primary registry recognized by the World Health Organization (WHO), established to provide a platform for registering clinical trials conducted in India. Launched in 2007, CTRI aims to enhance transparency, accountability, and ethical standards in clinical research. It serves as a comprehensive database, allowing researchers, healthcare professionals, and the public to access information about ongoing and completed trials. By promoting the registration of trials, CTRI helps ensure patient safety and encourages the ethical conduct of research in India.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A registry for clinical trials has been initiated by the ICMR’s National Institute of Medical Statistics (NIMS) and will involve registration of all clinical trials conducted in India so that the information collected are useful to health researchers, academicians, pharmaceutical industries and common man. The solution was to setup a registration portal for consolidating the data pertaining to clinical trials conducted by various agencies. The registry will be able to accept information over the Internet from accredited registrants and provide this information to any person desirous of obtaining information with respect to clinical trials. </p>','National Institute of Medical Statistics','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:48:41','A'),(57,'Others','Sanjeevani','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Hospital Information Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kaduvayil Thangal Charitable Trust Hospital (KTCTH) is a 250-bed facility providing both in-patient and outpatient services, catering to over 500 outpatients daily. Operated by a charitable trust, it offers affordable healthcare to economically weaker sections of society in the region. The hospital\'s functional and administrative processes were managed manually, from patient registration to discharge and billing, leading to cumbersome administration and challenges in information retrieval. To address these issues, the hospital decided to implement a Total Software Solution to automate its administrative and functional areas, improving efficiency and service delivery.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A detailed study conducted by a team of consultants identified 13 activities amenable for computerisation. The modules identified were Patient Registration, Patient Billing, Pharmacy Management, Ward Management, Laboratory Information System, Reimbursement Management, Inventory Control (General Stores), Contracts & Utility Management, Asset Management, Employee Information System, Leave Management, Payroll Management, and Financial Accounting. </p>','KTCT Hospital','KTCT',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:52:49','A'),(58,'General Administration','PIMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Personnel Information Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Factories & Boilers is the statutory authority for implementing statutes meant to improve the Safety, Welfare and Health of factory personnel in the State. The department was involved in the activities primarily related with issue & renewal of licenses to factories. It is a tedious task for the inspectors to manually keep track of the licensing procedures. The priority was to build up databases for all activities related to factories & boilers in the state.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">During the initial phases of computerization, the Directorate of Factories and Boilers automated its functional areas and consolidated data from across the state. To further enhance efficiency, the decision was made to automate HR functions by developing a Personnel Information and Management System. This comprehensive solution will include software applications for personnel information, file management, payroll, and transfers & postings. The effective use of IT in these areas expects a significant improvement in efficiency and reduce workload within the Directorate.</p>','Directorate of Factories & Boilers','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:17:35','A'),(59,'Others','QUEST','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Structured archival of Non Destructive Testing (NDT) data','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO), under the Department of Space, is India\'s premier agency for space research, with multiple establishments across the country. The Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) Laboratory in Trivandrum, Kerala, plays a crucial role in testing all rocket components throughout their life cycle before assembly for launch.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The NDT lab generates a substantial volume of data during the testing process, which is analysed by experienced scientists for clearance before launch. However, the lengthy testing procedures consume significant time from senior scientists, and the observations made are not easily retrievable for junior scientists, who often must re-examine the entire process.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">QUEST is a software for the structured archival of Non Destructive Testing (NDT) data. The solution is a Knowledgebase for radiographic analysis. The skill and experience of users accumulated over the years can be captured into a Knowledgebase The solution, Quest, converts the data / observations / comments etc. of the senior scientists into categorised sections and stores it in a database. It is possible for junior scientists to go through the complete process when he / she is making an inspection in the absence of a senior scientist. The software also has the provision for rule based analysis of defect data.</p>','VSSC, Indian Space Research Organisation','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:55:59','A'),(60,'Others','ARAM','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Automated Repayment and Allotment Management','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Kerala State Industrial Infrastructure Corporation Ltd. (Kinfra) is a Government of Kerala undertaking focused on developing industrial estates across the state for leasing to industrial units. Currently, Kinfra operates 11 industrial parks catering to various sectors, with new parks being regularly added. Kinfra acquires large tracts of land, develops them for specific industrial purposes, and offers options for purchase or long-term leases.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The organization manages numerous applicants for plots and sheds while tracking repayments from existing units. However, the varying processes for allotment and repayment across different parks and sectors make it challenging to maintain consistency and accuracy, especially as new parks are added.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A software solution for Repayment and Allotment Monitoring was recommended following a detailed study at Kinfra. The software solution, ARAM, is designed to keep track of the applicants to various units in each park and ensure the compliance of all formalities before a unit is allocated to an applicant. ARAM also manages the periodic repayments by the various units in the different parks. The software solution generates the monthly repayment schedule for each unit based on the approved interest rate for the park / industry sector. </p>','Kerala Industrial Infrastructure Development Corporation','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:57:40','A'),(61,'Others','CRIMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Crime Investigation Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Crime Branch Department of Kerala Police investigates approximately 1,000 cases annually, with special investigative units deployed across the state. Each case is assigned to a specific unit based on its nature and location, and is handled by an exclusive team that meticulously documents relevant information. The investigation process can be lengthy due to the labor-intensive data collection and reporting procedures. A fully manual system was in place to report case status from the field to headquarters which has become inadequate with time.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A software solution designed to monitor the progress of investigation was developed and deployed for the Crime Branch Department. The solution puts in place a reporting mechanism by which the investigative officers were able update the status of cases handled by them. The Crime Branch Headquarters can generate various reports to monitor the progress of investigation at each Investigating unit in the state. Reports can also be generated of the progress on each case and also the complete investigation details of the individual case. </p>','Kerala Police','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 10:58:27','A'),(62,'Others','School Management System','N','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','School Management System',NULL,'v','Love Dale School ','',NULL,'2024-07-30 18:49:46','A'),(63,'Others','CANES','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Campus Area Network and Enterprise Software ','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The National Institute of Health & Family Welfare (NIHFW), established under the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, promotes health and family welfare activities in India through education, training, research, evaluation, consultancy, and specialized services. Its key focus areas include Health Management, Communication, Health Systems Research, Training Technology, Health Economics, and Documentation. Previously, over 200 computers at the institute were mostly stand-alone or partially networked, resulting in isolated information silos with minimal data sharing. Most functions were carried out manually, limiting effective communication and collaboration among users.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Campus Area Network and Enterprise Software (CANES) project involved implementing a robust Network Backbone for the National Institute of Health & Family Welfare using Optic Fibre Cable (OFC) to connect various buildings on campus. Switched Local Area Networks (LANs) were established in each building, seamlessly linking computers across the institute. Additionally, a suite of software applications was developed to automate key functional and administrative activities. These applications are centrally deployed on servers, allowing users to access their respective modules from anywhere within the network.</p>','National Institute of Health & Family Welfare','New Delhi',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:05:02','A'),(64,'Others','Marketing Store Management Software','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Product Inventory, Sales and Marketing Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Trivandrum Regional Co-operative Milk Producers Union (TRCMPU) is a Kerala government owned organization engaged in the procurement, processing and sale of milk and milk products. A large number of products are produced and marketed by the TRCMPU under the umbrella brand MILMA. The Central Marketing Store is the central distribution point of the organization. Apart from the inventory the store maintains the details of each product sold through the different channels. The Central Marketing Store generates the various reports needed for market analysis by the top management. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The software solution implemented consists of three major modules namely Product Inventory, Sales and Marketing. Product inventory takes care of inventory management and is integrated to Sales module. It generates consolidated reports of inventory position on a daily basis. The Sales Application handles the sales through various channels. All the cash transactions related to sales are maintained in the software. The Marketing Information System aids the management in taking useful decisions by analysing the various aspects of sales.</p>','Trivandrum Regional Co-operative Milk Producers Union ','Trivandrum',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:07:35','A'),(65,'Others','MarBil','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Markerting and Billing Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Asianet Cable Vision (ACV) is headquartered in Thiruvananthapuram and operates 36 centres across the state, primarily managed by Video Service Providers (VSPs). A significant portion of ACV\'s revenue is generated from commercial advertisements. The marketing team prepares commercial proposals based on client inquiries and checks the availability of requested time slots. Upon receiving a Release Order from a client, they generate an internal Release Order for the studio, detailing the necessary particulars. After the advertisement is aired, a Telecast Confirmation Certificate (TCC) is issued, followed by the preparation of the corresponding invoice.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A workflow-based solution was put in place wherein all the three departments viz. Studio, Marketing and Accounts had access to the same information online. Once updated by the studio, the schedule of programs is instantaneously available to the marketing personnel. It is also possible to view the advertisements scheduled during a program. Once the marketing section captures the details of a new order, the information is available to the studio for scheduling purposes. On airing of the commercial, the accounts department is able to generate the invoices and the marketing personnel can follow up on the payment with the client. </p>','Asianet Cable Vision ','Asianet',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:09:34','A'),(66,'Others','Edify','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Teachers Training Monitoring ','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Directorate of Public Instruction (DPI) in Kerala is the key authority managing the state\'s education system under the Department of Education. It oversees school administration, teacher recruitment and training, curriculum development, and the evaluation of educational standards. DPI is committed to promoting inclusive education and ensuring accessibility for all students, regardless of socio-economic backgrounds. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">IT@SCHOOL is a project initiated by the Directorate of Public Instruction, Government of Kerala, aimed at integrating Information Technology into high school education to enhance the conventional teaching and learning system. This software keeps track of the personal and service information for each teacher undergoing IT training across the state.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Information collected during the training program will be entered into the system using pre-designed formats. The software also maintains detailed records of the schools involved and will have the capability to generate various reports, including data on teachers by institution, district, and state.</p>','Directorate of Public Instruction','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:10:56','A'),(67,'Others','CAMS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Common Admission Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Commissionerate of Entrance Examinations (CEE) is the sole agency set up by Government of Kerala to conduct Entrance Examinations for admission to various professional courses offered in Government and Private colleges in the state. The Commissionerate of Entrance Examinations conducts a joint Entrance Examination every year for admission to professional courses like Engineering, Medicine, Agriculture, Veterinary etc. Based on the common rank list the Commissionerate gives admission to the various seats in the colleges. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The software solution Common Admission Management System (CAMS), streamlined the process of admission management. The solution automates the process of determining the eligibility for admission based on conditions like rank for the relevant stream, minimum marks for the qualifying exam, age, reservation eligibility, selected course and selected college. As the system eliminates human intervention completely, the admission process became totally transparent leading to better confidence in the system and reducing litigation. The software also facilitated the process of multi-site admissions thereby shortening drastically the time taken for completing the whole admission process.</p>','Commissionerate of Entrance Examination (CEE)','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:11:55','A'),(68,'Others','HRIS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Health Research Information System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The National Institute of Medical Statistics (NIMS) is a nodal agency set up under Indian Council of Medical Research to help coordinate and standardize the collection of Medical and Health Statistics in the country. The institute provides statistical services and assistance to Central, State and Local Bodies in the field of Health, Medicine, Epidemiology and other allied areas. The institute also keeps track of the various research, training and other activities conducted across the many health related institutes in the country. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Health Research Information System (HRIS), is a repository of information on Research Projects, Publications, Training Programs, Seminars, Workshops and Conferences. The Software application was built on 3 Tier Architecture and designed for hosting over the Internet. Developed as a workflow based application, the users from any institution in the country can access and/or update information based on authorisation. </p>','National Institute of Medical Statistics (NIMS) ','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:12:45','A'),(69,'Others','Data Migration','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Migration of data from VLC Ssytem','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Office of the Accountant General, Kerala State at Thiruvananthapuram manages all accounts related to Government and Government personnel in the state. These responsibilities are administered from Trivandrum and also from the regional offices at Kottayam, Ernakulam, Thrissur and Kozhikode. The organization implemented Voucher Level Computerization a few years ago. The Voucher Level Computerisation (VLC) is implemented in all the 5 locations of the organization. Voucher information relating to all Government transactions are updated on the software.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Over a period of time, the VLC software application had become very slow due to the heavy build-up of data. It was beginning to take a long time to generate even routine reports from the application. The existing software was ported from the existing servers to newly acquired servers of higher processing capability. The data from the earlier server was also ported to the new server. The installation of the software application and porting of data was done at each of the five locations of the Office of the Accountant General. </p>','Office of the Accountant General','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:13:55','A'),(70,'Others','Archive Management','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Archive Management','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Office of the Accountant General in Thiruvananthapuram has five main departments: Pension, Provident Fund, Gazetted Entitlement, Accounts, and General Administration. It manages all accounts related to government personnel and handles Provident Fund and Pension details. Each year, the office generates around 100,000 files, with about half being pension-related. The files in process were stored in their respective sections, while closed files are archived for varying periods. These archived files are only retrieved when needed for reference. However, the accumulation of files in the Archives Section has made it challenging to locate specific documents. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Based on a detailed study conducted, it was proposed to implement a software solution to keep track of the Closed Files, Indexing Details, Re-issue details and Final Disposal. The proposed solution would have specific modules for Indexing, Transfer to Archives, Registration at Archive, Requisition for Referencing, Transfer to Section & Back to Archive, Permanent Disposal and Reports. The proposed solution is on open technologies and can be accessed from anywhere in the network. Users can search and submit requisition for retrieval of files for referencing.</p>','Office of the Accountant General','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:16:05','A'),(71,'Others','Total Automation','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Office Automation Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">M/s Kurian Abraham Ltd. is amongst the largest manufacturers and processors of centrifuged latex in India. Major activities include production of various forms of processed latex forms as well as finished products like examination and surgical gloves. The head office is at Kottayam and the administrative office is at Nagercoil. The three factories are located in and around Nagercoil. Having multiple offices and production centres, the marketing department finds it very difficult to reconcile orders in hand and the production status of its factories.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Based on a detailed study conducted, it was proposed to set up a private network connecting all the locations to the Head Office and generating various marketing related reports. The solution provides the respective users in the Marketing Department with information on Sales, Order Status, Order Processing and a wide range of reports. The information pertaining to marketing activities from the receipt of an enquiry to the point of product dispatch can be maintained in the system. Once implemented, a wide range of parameterised reports can be generated from the system.</p>','Kurian Abraham Ltd','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:17:30','A'),(72,'Others','Retail Management','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Billing, Inventory Management, CRM and Financial Accounting','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Parthas is a leading textile showroom in Kerala with an annual turnover exceeding Rs. 1 billion, stocking products from top brands across six floors and multiple billing points. Currently, activities are tracked through manual registers, making it challenging for management to analyse profitability, identify fast and slow-moving items, and understand customer profiles and re-visits. Due to increasing competition, the management recognizes the need for a software solution to provide essential information for informed decision-making.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Based on a detailed study conducted, the proposed software solution comprises of multiple modules for Billing, Inventory Management, Customer Relationship Management and Financial Accounting. The software facilitates Single Point Billing complying with the Value Added Tax (VAT) Rules. The Inventory software identifies slow, medium and fast moving stock, the quantity and sizes of a particular type of garment etc. for taking appropriate decisions. Customer Relationship Management module enables the creation of a Customer Database integrated with customer loyalty card. </p>','Parthas','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:20:11','A'),(73,'Others','VeTIS','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Vehicle Theft Information System ','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Kerala Police Department faces a significant challenge with high vehicle theft case registrations across the state. Each case requires extensive record-keeping, including details about complainants, vehicle owners, accused individuals, and recovery information. As the volume of cases grows, managing these records manually has become increasingly difficult. It also hinders timely information sharing among offices, delaying responses and efforts to apprehend culprits. A more efficient solution is urgently needed to streamline operations and enhance collaboration.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Vehicle Theft Information System (VeTIS) was designed to tackle the challenges of managing vehicle theft cases. This software consolidates all details previously kept in manual registers, allowing users to easily search for specific information online. Deployed on a central server, VeTIS ensures that every department office can access the database anytime, eliminating data duplication and making information available to authorized users statewide. VeTIS also features the ability to store photographs, fingerprints, and physical characteristics of gang members—covering attributes like hair, nose, ears, face, teeth, and eyes. </p>','Kerala Police','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:21:06','A'),(74,'Others','Amber','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','State-wide Data Consolidation Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The \"Kerala State Beverages (M & M) Corporation\" (KSBC) is a Public Sector Enterprise owned by the Govt. of Kerala and is the sole distributor for Alcoholic Products in the State. KSBC has 14 warehouses across the state from which nearly 250 retail outlets are being serviced. With a distributed model of buying, stocking and reselling, access to information on demand is a major factor for effective management. Though the organization had put in place an IT infrastructure that provides the top management with macro level information, it was difficult to get micro level information on demand. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Data from retail outlet billing machines were uploaded to the warehouse server, where it gets consolidated and used to generate reports for warehouse managers. This consolidated data is then transferred to the Central Server at the Head Office, enabling the generation of comprehensive reports from all warehouses. The software has two versions: one for the Head Office, focused on data consolidation from warehouses, and another for warehouses, which consolidates data from retail outlet transactions. Authorized personnel at the Head Office can access this vital information seamlessly.</p>','Kerala State Beverages (M & M) Corporation (KSBC)','Kerala State',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:22:58','A'),(75,'Others','Production Planning ','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Production Management Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Primus Gloves Pvt. Ltd is an export-oriented manufacturer producing 6 million premium medical gloves monthly. They currently rely on a manual data entry system for process control, capturing data from production to packing to ensure quality. The EDP section manages information needs, but many areas remain uncomputerized. To support their expansion, the management has tasked Kran with conducting a comprehensive study to develop a project report for an integrated software solution.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The study conducted at Primus Gloves Pvt. Ltd, in consultation with end users, highlighted critical gaps in information availability for informed decision-making. The initial plan focuses on automating core production and quality control processes, with production planning, purchasing, stores, and marketing slated for later stages. The proposed solution aims to streamline the entire process, capturing data from the moment gloves are removed from the production line to when they are packed for delivery, including details from the dryer and shop floor.</p>','Primus Gloves Pvt. Ltd.','Primus Gloves',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:36:47','A'),(76,'Others','CHOICE','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Election Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Office of the Chief Electoral Officer (CEO) in Kerala manages the state’s vast elector database, which includes over 25 million eligible voters. The office continuously enrols new voters and updates records by removing those who have moved or passed away, supported by 14 district sub-offices. Given the complexity of managing such a dynamic database—containing names, ages, addresses, and photographs—there is a strong need for computerization to streamline the process and enhance efficiency.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The CHOICE software solution has been implemented in the 14 sub-offices of the Chief Electoral Officer in Kerala, revolutionizing the creation, updating, and maintenance of the electoral database. This system securely stores comprehensive details of each elector, including photographs, fingerprints, and signatures, and facilitates the issuance of photo ID cards. With powerful search utilities, CHOICE helps filter duplicate names, reducing the risk of database tampering. It automates critical functions such as preparing electoral rolls, managing updates (additions, deletions, modifications), handling revisions, printing rolls, creating CD ROMs, archiving data, and overseeing the electors\' photo ID program.</p>','Office of the Chief Electoral Officer (CEO)','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:38:09','A'),(77,'Others','Kerala Fiscal Reforms','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Revamping of Treasury System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the Government of Kerala, all departmental expenses are processed through Treasuries and monitored by the Department of Finance. With numerous treasuries and departments, generating meaningful reports from the existing software had become challenging. To address this, the Kerala Fiscal Reforms proposed a revamp of the Treasury System, enabling the Department of Finance to generate comprehensive reports and better monitor the state\'s financial position. The goal is to study the current system and recommend changes to the database design for improved data capture and reporting.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A detailed study was conducted at the State Treasury, one District Treasury and one Sub Treasury to understand the present software design and architecture. The design was evaluated in detail to identify the inadequacies of the existing database design. Detailed discussions were also held with the senior officers of the Department of Finance. Based on the study all the drawbacks and inadequacies noticed were thoroughly documented. A new database design along with the suggestions to overcome the identified inadequacies was suggested to take care of the needs of the organisation.</p>','Department of Finance','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:40:00','A'),(78,'Others','Edify','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Training Management System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Institute of Management in Government (IMG) is Kerala\'s leading training institute, responsible for coordinating and standardizing training functions. Initially managing programs efficiently, IMG became the designated training provider in 2004 under the State Government\'s Modernizing Government Program, which emphasized employee retraining. This shift led to over 2,000 short-term and long-term courses being conducted annually. To address the increased workload and staff shortages, IMG has decided to automate routine and repetitive tasks, allowing personnel to focus on more productive work.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The proposed solution was to implement an Academic Program and Resource Management Software. The software maintains the details of the various organizations whose employees are to be trained, list of personnel in each of the offices, a database of training programs, details of faculty, venue etc. Facility is provided for the course coordinator to schedule the program, request for resources, generate invitation lists etc. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Once a course is scheduled the necessary resources are blocked and the information is automatically made available to all the concerned personnel in the organization. Each resource manager will then be able to schedule his/her respective programs based on the current availability of resources. </p>','Institute of Management in Government (IMG)','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:41:07','A'),(79,'Others','Workflow Automation','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Process workflow automation','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Koncherry Coir Factories is a leading manufacturer of trendy floor coverings and one of India\'s largest exporters of jute, hemp, and polypropylene rugs. The company sources high-quality raw materials both locally and internationally, outsourcing work to skilled weavers and subcontractors. With stringent quality control on finished products, Koncherry exports to clients worldwide. However, the entire process is currently managed manually, making it challenging to monitor activities and implement timely corrections. To facilitate growth, the management is now exploring automation of documentation processes across various departments.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Based on a detailed study conducted, a software solution was proposed that automates the workflow related to marketing, production, purchase, dying, sampling and packing sections of the organisation so that information is made available on demand to concerned personnel. Once the primary data gets captured, the software can automatically generate all the forms/reports that are being currently manually entered/created. In addition, various production and analytical reports too can be generated. Upon implementation, the software will meet all the functional requirements of a typical process flow industry to a large extent.</p>','Koncherry Coir Factories','Koncherry Coir Factories',NULL,'2024-11-15 11:42:04','A'),(80,'Others','Commercial Carpet Survey ','Y','N','N','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','N','Online Product Survey System','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">DProbe is a software services company based in the USA specialising in market research applications. As part of servicing its clients Dprobe provides web-based data collection and information generation from a select sample population. Due to its limited project management resources, the company routinely outsources its jobs to other countries around the world.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Commercial Carpet Survey Project was one of the projects outsourced by dProbe to Kran Consulting. The project envisaged setting up a web portal for conducting a survey on the perception of persons responsible for purchasing carpets either for themselves or for their clients. The survey was an attempt to study the commercial carpet market and to identify various related parameters.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">As the target segment lived far apart from each other in various states, it was decided that an online survey would have the best chance for collecting the most accurate data. A detailed survey questionnaire was designed for the purpose. The target respondents were identified and their details collated.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The target respondents were given the link to access the survey questionnaire page. Once authenticated the respondents would be taken in a sequential manner through each question of the questionnaire based on the need of the survey. The respondent on answering the question will also be able to see the results of the survey on a continuous basis.</p>','DProbe','DProbe',NULL,'2024-11-15 12:34:53','A'),(81,'Others','Akshaya','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Email Administration & Web site Maintenance','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Akshaya project envisages the use of Information Communication Technologies as a catalyst for economic and social development. The project was a success and Malappuram became the first IT literate district in the country. There was constant demand for more local content on the website for rural population. Also, frequent updations to the website became very much relevant.</p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Akshaya Project leverages Information Communication Technologies to drive economic and social development. To enhance the website for the rural population, there was a growing demand for more local content and frequent updates. Key modifications were identified, including the establishment of email services for better communication with moderators, presentations, and publicity materials. To address these needs, the Akshaya website was updated daily, ensuring new information is posted within 24 hours. Additionally, approximately 750 email IDs were created and managed as part of the services. </p>','Kerala State IT Mission','Govt. of Kerala',NULL,'2024-11-15 12:35:52','A'),(82,'Others','Legacy Data Migration','Y','N','N','N','N','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','Data Migration of Accounts Data','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">KERAFED is a co-operative organisation under the Government of Kerala engaged in the business of producing and marketing coconut oil. Kerafed had a computerized financial accounting package. This solution was developed on Power Builder 5.0 and the database was on Integra Version 4.0. The operating system used was SCO Unix Version 3.1. The database Integra had many disadvantages. It was relatively slow, lacked trained manpower, support was not available on time, RDBMS engine was not flexible enough. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">To overcome the disadvantages that persisted with the existing software it was found necessary to migrate to Oracle RDBMS. The operating system was changed to Windows NT, keeping pace with the changes in technology. The front end for the software was reworked using Developer 2000. The software aids in migrating the existing software application module on Integra / Unix to Oracle / NT. The application was designed on Developer 2000 with Oracle as its backend.</p>','KERAFED','KERAFED',NULL,'2024-11-15 12:39:07','A'),(83,'Enterprise Resource Planning','eAdmin','Y','N','N','Y','Y','Y','N','N','N','N','N','N','Administrative ERP Solution','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">‘NORKA - ROOTS’, an establishment of Government of Kerala is an agency set up to take care of the welfare of the Non-Resident Keralites. The organization is headquartered in Trivandrum and has presence in major cities in Kerala. Apart from managing the welfare schemes initiated by the state government for the non-resident Keralites (NRKs) as a group, the organization also takes up projects in association with individual NRKs. NORKA – ROOTS, having been recently formed, is in the process of implementing systems and procedures for streamlining internal processes and project administration. </p>','<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The implemented solution comprises of a suite of software applications, which automates the core administrative and functional operations of the organization. This ensures that the organization is effectively administered as a compact entity. The software modules implemented at NORKA – ROOTS as part of the project are Attendance Management, Financial Accounting, Asset Register, Visitors’ Register, Entrepreneurship Development and File Tracking & Processing Solution. All routine reports that were being generated manually are now generated automatically from the respective software modules.</p>','NORKA-ROOTS','Govt. of India',NULL,'2024-11-05 13:35:53','A');
