INSERT INTO `project_product` VALUES (1,'FINASSAM FOR FINANCE DEPT. GOVERNMENT OF ASSAM','The Directorate of Factories & Boilers is the statutory authority for implementing statutes meant to improve the Safety, Welfare and Health of factory personnel in the Sate. The department is involved in the activities primarily related with issue & renewal of licenses to factories.','FinAssam is the Financial Management Information System (FMIS) implemented for Government of Assam which consolidates all the financial information needs of the state government into one information database. It is an Integrated Financial Management System for the state of Assam with modules like Budget Planning & Preparation, Budget Modification, Budget Distribution, Treasury Bills, Administrative Approvals, Technical Sanctions, Financial Sanctions, Fixation of Ceilings, NPS, RIDF, Debt Management, First Salary, Employee Self Service etc. It also comprise of value added modules like SDG aligned Outcome Budget, e Budget etc. FinAssam project is also integrated with RBI, NPS, PFMS etc. It is a World Bank funded project.','Project','0.7660699401807328@-@idms.jpg','A','Software Development',67),(2,'PARESHRAM FOR LABOUR DEPT. GOVERNMENT OF ODISHA','National Safai Karamcharis Finance & Development Corporation (NSKFDC), a wholly owned Govt. of India Undertaking was set up as a Company “Not for Profit. NSKFDC is an Apex Corporation for the all-round socio-economic up-liftment of the Safai Karamcharis, Scavengers and their dependants throughout India, through various loan and non-loan based schemes. NSKFDC has been designated as the Nodal Agency for implementation of the Central Sector Self Employment Scheme for Rehabilitation of Manual Scavengers (SRMS) under the aegis of the Ministry of Social Justice & Empowerment.','PAReSHRAM is a unified service delivery platform implemented for the Labour& ESI Department, Govt. of Odisha that aids as an effective tool to deliver services in a timely, cost-effective and transparent manner to both internal and external stakeholders and help improve the \"Ease of Doing Business\". Various citizen services offered by both the Directorate of Labour and the Directorate of Factories & Boilers are made fully online along with e-payment, tracking and notification features. With such a system in place, the applicants are able to submit applications without visiting the offices, and the overall speed of the service delivery has enhanced drastically. The certificates issued by the department are bar coded and can be verified from the portal, either by providing the tracking number or certificate number. In brief, it is a major transformation whereby the need for physical touch points and paper based processing was completely done away with.','Project','0.22739460558247482@-@nskfdc.jpg','A','Software Development',68),(3,'RISE FOR SANTACRUZ ELECTRONICS EXPORT PROCESSING ZONE','National Backward Classes Finance & Development Corporation (NBCFDC) incorporated \r\nas a Company not for profit with an objective to promote economic and developmental activities for the benefit of Backward Classes and to assist the poorer section of these classes in skill development and self employment ventures. NBCFDC extends loans to State Channelizing Agencies (SCAs), who in turn provide concessional loans to persons belonging to Other Backward Classes (OBCs), living below the poverty line. The Corporation also extends training grant to these SCAs and other institutions for providing skill development training to the target group.\r\n','It is an Enterprise Class Solution “RISe” for the end-to-end automation of its functional, administrative, financial, and managerial areas of SEEPZ SEZ. The solution aids in bringing oa transformative change in the way SEEPZ manage their operations. With advanced features, robust security, and streamlined processes, the solution stands as a catalyst for efficiency, transparency, and compliance in the dynamic landscape of SEEPZ. It comprises of key modules like Estate Management including Land and Building (Fixed Assets), Financial Accounting Management, Unit Management, UAC (Unit Approval Committee), Rate, Rent & Bills management, Security Contract Management, Waste Disposal Monitoring, Contract Performance Monitoring, Conference Room Management, Guest House Management, Creche Management etc.','Project','0.9889504153503785@-@nbcfdc.jpg','A','Software Development',69),(4,'BI, DEBT & AUDIT SOLUTION FOR FINANCE DEPT., GOVT. OF JHARKHAND','“ The Kerala State Audit Department is under the administrative control of the Finance Department, Govt. of Kerala. The Directorate conducts the audit of Local Self Government Institutions and Local Funds included in the schedule of the Kerala Local Fund Audit Act 1994 and management of the corpus of Charitable Endowments in the state. ','The solution helps to build dashboards using BI Tool/ Analytics, Debt Management module, Audit Management module and Mobile Apps/ Platform. The solution is designed to analyse the output that helps in meaningful insights for various stakeholders to identify the actual pain areas and to improve upon for better fiscal governance. The dynamic dashboard using the proposed BI tool aids in easy and meaningful interpretation of the current and historical data. The Debt module maintains the up to date information pertaining to all the borrowings of the state. The Audit module keeps track of all the audit findings provided by the state Accountant General.','Project','0.13176740031568723@-@ksad.jpg','A','Software Development',70),(5,'FABOS FOR DIRECTORATE OF FACTORIES & BOILERS, GOVERNMENT OF KERALA','The Finance Department, Government of Assam initiated various projects to automate the processes with regard to \r\n•	Monitoring Financial Information\r\n•	Capturing Financial Transactions\r\n•	Facilitating Integration with other Stake Holders of the Department like AG, RBI and Agency Banks dealing with the State Government.\r\n','The solution automates the core Functional and Administrative areas of Factories and Boilers department including the public interfacing with the industries resulting in significant improvements in efficiency of the organization. It also helps to put in place an effective communication channel wherever applicable through E-Mail and SMS notifications to the stake holders. Digital signature and payment gateway integrations are also incorporated. A wide range of reports can be generated by the users based on authentication. The key modules facilitate Govt. to Business delivery. Factory Information System takes care of the grant of license, renewal, transfer, amendments etc. Boiler Information System handles registration, renewals, transfer, amendments etc.','Project','0.8744173251758124@-@goa.jpg','A','Software Development',71),(6,'AFEGU FOR FINANCE DEPARTMENT, GOVERNMENT OF ASSAM','The Finance Department, Government of Assam initiated various projects to automate the processes with regard to –\r\n•	Monitoring Financial Information\r\n•	Capturing Financial Transactions\r\n•	Facilitating Integration with other Stake Holders of the Department like AG, RBI and Agency Banks dealing with the State Government.\r\n','Various IT projects were already initiated by the department and was under different stages of implementation. To streamline the implementation of the ongoing projects, and to initiate newer projects within the department, an exclusive e-Governance Unit was setup within the Finance Department. Consultancy was provided for “IT Consulting and Technical Support Services” for the e-Governance unit.','Project','0.7573291323119627@-@0.3444953853460526@-@goa.jpg','A','Consultancy',46),(7,'AFEGU for Finance Department, Government of Assam','The Finance Department, Government of Assam initiated various projects to automate the processes with regard to –\r\n•	Monitoring Financial Information\r\n•	Capturing Financial Transactions\r\n•	Facilitating Integration with other Stake Holders of the Department like AG, RBI and Agency Banks dealing with the State Government.\r\n','Various IT projects were already initiated and was under different stages of implementation. To streamline the implementation of the ongoing projects, and to initiate newer projects within the Department, an exclusive E-Governance Unit was setup within the Finance Department. Consultancy was provided for “IT Consulting and Technical Support Services” for the e-Governance unit. ','Project','0.780971123515594@-@goa.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',54),(8,'NIRMANSHRAMIK FOR ODISHA BUILDING & OTHER CONSTRUCTION WORKERS WELFARE BOARD','Kerala State Women Development Corporation (KSWDC), is a Public Sector Organization set up by Government of Kerala. The Corporation was set up with the specific purpose of achieving the Economic Empowerment of the Women in the state.','It is a centralized workers welfare management system that helps in ensuring the timely delivery of eligible benefits to the registered building & other construction workers of the state. It is a digital platform that facilitates Registration (of Workers, Principal Employers), Generation of QR Code based ID Card, Submission of requests (for Pension, Maternity Benefit etc.), Processing of Applications, Approvals/Rejections, Fee Collection, Cess Collection, Fund Management, Benefit Disbursal etc. The solution is integrated with the Payment Gateway, Email / SMS Gateway, Digital Signature etc.','Project','0.18153244529845924@-@kswdc.jpg','A','Software Development',72),(9,'Kerala State Women Development Corporation','Kerala State Women Development Corporation (KSWDC), is a Public Sector Organization set up by Government of Kerala. The Corporation was set up with the specific purpose of achieving the Economic Empowerment of the Women in the state.','The project is to implement a web based solution that automates the core functional activities of KSWDC. Once deployed, it will result in significant improvements in handling the core functions of the Organization. Development of application s/w, configuration & implementation, End user training and System Administrator training were the part of the contract. S/ W application is meant for the full functional automation of the corporation. The s/w will facilitate the Senior Officers to view the current status of any Project / Scheme / File etc.','Project','0.5549747061599064@-@kswdc.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',55),(10,'CHANAKYA FOR DIRECTORATE OF ECONOMICS & STATISTICS, ASSAM','','The solution is to facilitate software enabled preparation of Macro Fiscal Projection for the State of Assam. The envisaged solution comprises of two modules namely 1) Macro Fiscal Aggregates and 2) Macro Fiscal Projection. Macroeconomic projections aim to predict and understand the future state of the economy on a broad scale. It includes information related to economic growth, inflation, wages, unemployment and trade.','Project','0.7354703652914284@-@fims.jpg','A','Software Development',73),(11,'FIMS FOR FINANCE INSPECTION WING, KERALA','','Finance Inspection Wing was constituted in Finance Department in 1964 to ensure that financial rules and procedures are scrupulously followed by the departmental officers. The Inspection Party will conduct surprise inspection of Government Offices and report to Government cases of irregularity, slackness or indifference shown by Heads of Departments or Offices in the matter of financial control. The Inspection Party is empowered to scrutinize all files and registers relating to accounts, stores and other allied matters. They are also empowered to conduct physical verification of cash and stores wherever deemed necessary. All Heads of Departments and Offices shall give the inspection staff necessary co-operation and facilities for the proper discharge of their functions. The Inspection Party will submit their reports to the Secretary to Government in the Finance Department, who will decide the follow up action to be taken on the reports. It is proposed to computerise the key activities of the Finance Inspection Wing thereby facilitate the achievement of goals like complete and precise documentation of inspections, timely inspections, repeat inspections, effective management of follow up actions etc.','Project','0.6123906987149641@-@fims.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',56),(12,'AIMS FOR KERALA STATE AUDIT DEPARTMENT','The Directorate of Audit (Local Fund) is under the administrative control of the Finance Department, Govt. of Kerala. The Directorate conducts the audit of Local Self Government Institutions and Local Funds included in the schedule of the Kerala Local Fund Audit Act 1994 and management of the corpus of Charitable Endowments in the state. The Director is assisted by 3 Joint Directors, 2 Deputy Directors and 13 Audit Officers at the Directorate. There are 14 district level offices under the control of the Deputy Directors of Local Fund Audit. It also conducts the audit of Panchayats, Municipal Councils, Miscellaneous and Grant-in-aid Institutions etc. Also concurrent audit is carried out in Municipal Corporations, Universities and Institutions like Kerala State Housing Board, Kerala State Rural Development Board, State Institute of Languages, State Institute of Encyclopaedic Publications, Travancore and Guruvayoor Devaswom, Trivandrum Development Authority and Greater Cochin Development Authority.','This project was conceptualized, designed, developed and implemented catering to the key functional requirements of the Kerala State Audit Department. The key features of the solution comprise of Audit plan preparation and its approval, team scheduling, audit findings, final audit report, charge / surcharge certificates, memorandum of important points and audit monitoring. In brief, it helps to manage the entire lifecycle of a typical audit right from audit planning stage through its execution & reporting to its monitoring.','Project','0.9147636335878286@-@ksad.jpg','A','Software Development',74),(13,'AIMS FOR LOCAL FUND AUDIT DEPT, KERALA','The Directorate of Audit (Local Fund) is under the administrative control of the Finance Department, Govt. of Kerala. The Directorate conducts the audit of Local Self Government Institutions and Local Funds included in the schedule of the Kerala Local Fund Audit Act 1994 and management of the corpus of Charitable Endowments in the state. The Director is assisted by 3 Joint Directors, 2 Deputy Directors and 13 Audit Officers at the Directorate. There are 14 district level offices under the control of the Deputy Directors of Local Fund Audit. It also conducts the audit of Panchayats, Municipal Councils, Miscellaneous and Grant-in-aid Institutions etc. Also concurrent audit is carried out in Municipal Corporations, Universities and Institutions like Kerala State Housing Board, Kerala State Rural Development Board, State Institute of Languages, State Institute of Encyclopaedic Publications, Travancore and Guruvayoor Devaswom, Trivandrum Development Authority and Greater Cochin Development Authority. ','The solution Audit Information Management System “AIMS” intends to implement a web based solution that automates the core functional activities of the Directorate. It is believed that to a very large extent the proposed system will meet the automation requirements pertaining to the audit functions of the organization. The solution is work flow enabled wherein users will have different roles and responsibilities. Based on the roles assigned, the user will be able to access, view, modify, approve information submitted. The key features of the solution comprise of Audit plan preparation and its approval, team scheduling, audit findings, final audit report, charge / surcharge certificates, memorandum of important points and audit monitoring.','Project','0.2841168329893272@-@ksad.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',57),(14,'CTRI FOR NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF MEDICAL STATISTICS','','The project was to setup a registration portal for consolidating the data pertaining to clinical trials conducted by various agencies. The registry will be able to accept information over the Internet from accredited registrants and provide this information to any person desirous of obtaining information with respect to clinical trials. It is a full-fledged primary registry of India and the ultimate goal of the registry is to develop an electronically searchable web-based system that is accessible to the public free of cost.','Project','0.8704460050460829@-@bmsicl.jpg','A','Software Development',75),(15,'BMEDS FOR BIHAR MEDICAL SERVICES & INFRASTRUCTURE CORPORATION','','BMEDS – Bihar Medical Equipments and Drugs System for BMSICL is a web based solution built on open technologies that caters to the core functional automation needs of the organization. The solution is work flow enabled wherein users will have different roles and responsibilities. The key areas covered are drug procurement, quality check and its distribution, equipment procurement, allocation and its maintenance.','Project','0.29438796936393596@-@bmsicl.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',58),(16,'LEAP FOR NATIONAL BACKWARD CLASSES FINANCE DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, GOVERNMENT OF INDIA','','The solution automates the Loan & HR management activities of the organization. It also facilitates maintenance of information pertaining to grants given to Sector Skill Councils / Training Institutes for promoting training programs on entrepreneurship development. It will be a web based application and would be hosted on a central server. Modules include; Loan to SCA/CP (PSB/RRB/MFI) based on Lending Schemes, Grant to Sector Skill Councils based on Promotional Schemes, HR Management System, Management Information System and Technical Administration Module.','Project','0.2634756654399849@-@goa.jpg','A','Software Development',76),(17,'STAGE  FOR DIRECTORATE OF ACCOUNTS & TREASURY, ASSAM','The Directorate of Accounts & Treasury processes a large number of files every year. The sheer logistics defy conventional solutions. The efficiency of the organization more often than not, depends on the speedy and transparent processing of files. STAGE is an effective tool to address this need. It is proposed to implement a file processing and management solution for the Directorate.','“ Speedy and Transparent Administration in Government Establishments “STAGE” is a first step towards paperless office in the organization. The key features include registration & routing of inward correspondence, file creation, processing & routing, file linking, file closing & archiving, file tracking information, file take over facility, remote access over internet, remote document submission, knowledgebase, exhaustive search, stock file / stock tray, call book, reminder diary, notings, drafts, instant messaging. Various parameterized reports can be generated on demand. ','Project','0.4840448834312129@-@goa.jpg','A','Project / Product Implementation',63),(18,'FINANCE DEPT. AUTOMATION, GOVERNMENT OF ASSAM','“ With its central responsibility of ensuring prudent and efficient management of the State’s economy, Finance Department of the Assam State Government has a major role in managing and monitoring of public finance in the state. The efficiency with which the department conducts its own affairs, affects to a great extent, the efficiency of the other departments in the government also. In order to improve efficiency and to bring in transparency in its functioning, the department desires to implement computerisation on select areas where significant improvement in efficiency can be achieved and are amenable for automation.','The solution envisaged intends to automate the key activities of the Finance Department. The services include design and development of suggested software for the activities identified; its implementation, training, support, warranty and maintenance for a period of 12 months. The solution will be fully on open technologies. Further the solution will be server centric and only browser is required at the client end to access the system. The areas considered for the project are File Processing & Management, Project Monitoring, Repository of Acts, Rules & Regulations, Monitoring of CAG Reports, Monitoring of Inspection Reports & Monitoring of Policy Recommendations.','Project','0.820861411589129@-@goa.jpg','A','Project / Product Implementation',64),(19,'IFMS FOR FINANCE DEPARTMENT, GOVERNMENT OF ASSAM','As part of the Assam Governance and Public Resource Management Program (AGPRMP), the Government of Assam plans to implement an Integrated Government Financial Management Information System (IGFMIS).  IGFMIS involves the consolidation of information from multiple sources in various departments of the Government of Assam and also other agencies having financial transactions with the Government. IGFMIS has two major components viz. 1) Financial Management Information System (FMIS) and 2) Human Resources Management System (HRMS).','This was an ADB funded consultancy assignment with the prime object to implement an Integrated Financial Management System for the state. The consulting assignment covered the key objectives of IFMS like Present up-to-date, accurate and easily managed financial information, Provide regional financial information and statistics, Provide financial recording, control and the reporting of comprehensive quality, Provide effective financial monitoring and control, planning and direction of the financial resources of the state and Support formulation and control of state fiscal policy.','Project','0.603288310859488@-@goa.jpg','A','Consultancy',47),(20,'HRMS FOR GOVERNMENT OF ASSAM','The Directorate of Audit (Local Fund) is under the administrative control of the Finance Department. The Directorate conducts the audit of Local Fund Accounts in the state. It also conducts the audit of such other Non-Govt institutions and Govt. offices or any private institutions under the provisions of the certain Acts or Rules framed by the Govt. or under orders from the Government.\r\n\r\nConsidering the large number of accounts to be audited every year involving a very large number of personnel across the state, the volume of routine and repetitive work in the department is very high. In order to improve efficiency and to bring in transparency in its functioning, the department desires to implement computerisation on select areas where significant improvement in efficiency can be achieved and are amenable for automation. \r\n','This was an ADB funded consultancy assignment where it was envisaged to implement a centralized Human Resources Management System for Government of Assam. As part of this assignment, areas amenable for computerization were identified. The components of HRMS that were subjected to detailed study are Recruitment Management, Employee Information Management, Leave Management, Training Management, Transfers & Postings Management, Promotions Management, Payroll Management, Performance & Appraisal Management, and Competency & Skills Management.','Project','0.28907960167428204@-@goa.jpg','A','Consultancy',48),(21,'SMARTWINGS FOR INDIAN AIR FORCE','Indian Space Research Organization (ISRO) under Department of Space is the premier agency in India, which conducts various Space Research programs. The organization has multiple establishments specializing in various activities located in different places in India. The Non Destructive Testing (NDT) Laboratory of the organization is based in Trivandrum, Kerala State. All parts which go into the assembling of a rocket are brought to the NDT lab in Trivandrum and tested through its life cycle before being finally assembled for launch of the vehicle.\r\n\r\nThe volume of data that is generated is very high during the testing process. This data is analyzed by experienced scientists and then cleared for the launch. It was noted that, the many long hours of a senior scientist’s time and effort are lost with the testing of one specific part. The observations of the scientists are not easily retrievable at a later date by a junior scientist who is then forced to go through the entire process. \r\n','SmartWings is a software solution for office automation designed and developed to suit the requirements of No.5 Wing, Kalaikunda office of Indian Air Force. It has been customised to suit the exact needs of No. 5 Wing, Kalaikunda. It consists of two unique software products STAGE and INTRANET. While STAGE addresses the requirements of File Processing, INTRANET provides for the intra office communication between the users.','Project','0.853750269874431@-@isro.jpg','A','Software Development',77),(22,'SMARTWINGS” FOR NO.5 WING, IAF KALAIKUNDA','The No.5 Wing, Airforce Station is based in Kalaikunda, West Midnapore; West Bengal. No 5 Wing is a major station under Eastern Air Command of the Indian Air Force.\r\nThe No.5 Wing, Kalaikunda was keen on implementing a computerised solution for automating the entire file movement of the wing. It also needed a solution for effective communication between users within the organisation.\r\n','SmartWings is a software solution for office automation designed and developed to suit the requirements of a typical office. It has been customised to suit the exact needs of No. 5 Wing, Kalaikunda. It consists of two unique software products STAGE and INTRANET. While STAGE addresses the requirements of File Processing, INTRANET provides for the intra office communication between the users.”','Project','0.03637814502254688@-@isro.jpg','A','Project / Product Implementation',65),(23,'PHOENIX FOR KERALA STATE POLLUTION CONTROL BOARD','','The solution aids in the electronic service delivery to industries and establishments across the state of Kerala in terms of issuing Consent to Operate, Consent to Establish. It covers end to end functionalities of a typical citizen service portal such as one time registration, request for consent to operate / establish, request scrutiny and processing, e-payment, generation of consent certificate, renewal, amendment, transfer etc. The solution also covers other areas like Waste & Returns Management, Complaint Management, Laboratory Management, Legal Actions Management, Internal Communication & Collaboration Suite, Dashboard & MIS, Data Analytics and Mobile App. This project is one of the key initiatives for improving the Ease of Doing Business.','Project','0.18251757986401262@-@who.jpg','A','Software Development',78),(24,'ESMAC FOR KERALA STATE CO-OPERATIVE FEDERATION FOR FISHERIES DEVELOPMENT LTD','A registry for clinical trials has been initiated by the ICMR’s National Institute of Medical Statistics (NIMS) and will involve registration of all clinical trials conducted in India so that the information collected are useful to health researchers,  academicians, pharmaceutical industries and common man.','In order to offer better support to the fishermen community and also to administer the HR related activities of the organization effectively, it is required to have current and precise information on demand to all the concerned officials. The project is an Enterprise System covering the Loan & Human Resource (HR) management wherein information is shared amongst the Officials concerned, Employees and other Stakeholders based on role and authorization. The software comprises of two major modules namely Loan Management and Human Resource (HR) Management. The Loan Management module covers end to end functionalities right from Loan Application through its Processing, Sanction & Disbursement, Repayment, Recovery to its closure. It also covers Society Registration, One Time Settlement, Moratorium, Fund Management, and detailed MIS Reports. The Human Resource (HR) Management module includes a digital service book with sub modules like Leave, Payroll, Transfer & Postings, Promotions, Performance Appraisal, Disciplinary Actions etc.','Project','0.8268830248216998@-@goi.jpg','A','Software Development',79),(25,'SHESOFT FOR KERALA STATE WOMEN’S DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION','The National Institute of Medical Statistics (NIMS) is a nodal agency set up under Indian Council of Medical Research to help coordinate and standardize the collection of Medical and Health Statistics in the country. The institute provides statistical services and assistance to Central, State and Local Bodies in the field of Health, Medicine, Epidemiology and other allied areas. The institute also keeps track of the various research, training and other activities conducted across the many health related institutes in the country. Presently all such information compiled and collated from the various institutions are maintained in Manual Registers. This makes it difficult for the institute to provide prompt and accurate responses to specific queries from Government and other interested agencies. ','The project was to implement a web based solution that automates the core functional activities of KSWDC. The core function of loan management is automated as part of this project. It is a fully Integrated Work Flow enabled Loan Management System, primarily for NBFCs offering subsidized loans to specific target groups. The module covers the entire life cycle of the process starting from loan processing, disbursal and repayments. Apart from loan management, KSWDC has also automated its routine administrative areas like file management, asset management, employee service records, leave, payroll, training, hostel etc.','Project','0.4852635183195759@-@nims.jpg','A','Software Development',80),(26,'FIMS FOR FINANCE INSPECTION WING, KERALA','The Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (MOHFW) established National Health Account (NHA) Cell in collaboration with World Health Organization (WHO) in the year 2003.','Finance Inspection Management System (FIMS) was devised to computerise the key activities of the Finance Inspection Wing to facilitate the achievement of set objectives of the wing like complete and precise documentation of inspections, timely inspections, repeat inspections, effective management of follow up actions etc. FIMS is a solution that covers the functionalities related to inspection management which includes the preparation and approval of inspection schedules, inspection reports etc. It has the facility to prepare schedules of review meetings and to check the availability of participants. It includes file processing for correspondence other than inspection matters.','Project','0.9156404403729362@-@goi.jpg','D','Software Development',81),(28,'LIMS FOR NATIONAL SAFAI KARAMCHARIS FINANCE DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, GOVERNMENT OF INDIA','The Prison Headquarters is situated at Thiruvananthapuram and is headed by the Director General of Police, Prisons. An Ex-Cadre post of I.G.P (prisons) has been created to assist the DGP. The Head of the Department is assisted by the Southern Deputy Inspectors General. There are three Regional Offices, one in Kozhikode headed by Deputy Inspector General of Prisons who supervises the Northern Region and another in Thrissur to supervise the Central Region and the third in Thiruvananthapuram. There are 3 Central jails, 3 District Jails, 5 special jails, 28 sub jails, 2 open jails 1 women’s prison and one borstal school','The solution automates the Loan management activities of the organization. As a national funding agency the loans are provided to the State Channelizing Agencies and Regional Rural Banks. The solution covers details like Notional Allocation, Annual Action Plan from SCA / RRB, Guarantee Details, Sanction, Drawl Request, Disbursement, Repayment Schedule, Repayment Details, One Time Settlement, Demand Generation, Defaulters List, Notices, SMS / Email Reminders and Loan Closure.','Project','0.13836471289285468@-@jail.jpg','A','Software Development',82),(29,'DIRECTORATE OF AUDIT (LOCAL FUND), GOVERNMENT OF ASSAM','In Government of Kerala, all expenses incurred by any department / organization in the state are transacted through the Treasuries and is monitored by the Department of Finance. The transactions happen under the specific head of accounts at various Districts and Taluk Treasuries located across the state. Considering the number of treasuries, departments, offices etc., it was becoming difficult for the Department of Finance to generate meaningful reports from the existing software. As part of the Kerala Fiscal Reforms it was proposed to revamp the Treasury System to facilitate the generation of comprehensive reports by the Department of Finance so as to enable them to keep a close watch on the Financial Position of the state. The mandate was then to study the existing system and suggest necessary changes in the database design to capture additional data for generation of the necessary reports','It was envisaged to implement a software solution for managing the Audits being conducted by the Directorate. The scope of work was to provide consultancy in the preparation of the Software Requirement Specifications (SRS) for the management of Audits conducted by the Directorate. The SRS forms the basis for the development and implementation of the software.','Project','0.603288310859488@-@goa.jpg','A','Consultancy',49),(30,'CONSULTANCY SERVICE FOR KERALA FISCAL REFORMS','Primus Gloves Pvt. Ltd is an Export Oriented Unit manufacturing premium quality gloves with a production capacity of 6 million pieces of medical gloves per month. The company has put in place an elaborate process control system based on manual data entry of forms. Right from the time the gloves are stripped off the production line to the packing stage, a systematic and sequential system is followed to capture data and to control quality of the final product. The company has an EDP section that handles the information requirement of the management. Most of the functional areas are yet to be computerized. As part of their expansion project, the management commissioned Kran to conduct a detailed study for the preparation of a project report for an integrated software solution for the organization.','A detailed study was conducted at the State Treasury, one District Treasury and one Sub Treasury to understand the existing software design and architecture. The design was evaluated in detail to identify the inadequacies of the existing database design. Detailed discussions were also held with the senior officers of the Department of Finance. Based on the study all the drawbacks and inadequacies noticed were thoroughly documented. A new database design along with the suggestions to overcome the identified inadequacies was suggested to take care of the needs of the organization.','Project','0.08465754056513375@-@gok.jpg','A','Consultancy',50),(31,'PRODUCTION PLANNING FOR PRIMUS GLOVES','M/s Kurian Abraham Ltd. is amongst the largest manufacturers and processors of centrifuged latex in India. Major activities include production of various forms of processed latex forms as well as finished products like examination and surgical gloves. The head office is at Kottayam and the administrative office is at Nagercoil. The three factories are located in and around Nagercoil. Having multiple offices and production centers, the marketing department finds it very difficult to reconcile orders in hand and the production status of its factories','As part of this assignment, a detailed study was conducted at the organization in consultation with the end users, identified the gaps that exist in the need and availability of information for informed decision-making. Based on the study, a plan was drawn up to automate the core production and quality control processes in the first stage. Functional areas like production planning, purchase, stores and marketing were recommended for subsequent stages. These modules can be later dovetailed into the production and quality control processes. The solution proposed was to automate the entire process from the point where the gloves are stripped off the production line to the point where they are packed for delivery.','Project','0.8728229945151106@-@primus.jpg','A','Consultancy',51),(32,'CANES FOR NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF HEALTH & FAMILY WELFARE, GOVERNMENT OF INDIA','The Directorate of Public Relations (DPR) primarily handles the task of dissemination of information about the various Government Programs and compiles news items pertaining to public feedback from the Print and Electronic Media. Other responsibilities of the department includes conducting various awareness and mass contact programs on behalf of the State Government, issuing accreditation to Journalists, providing retirement benefits to journalists, issue of various tender advertisements on behalf of Government and Public Sector Undertakings. The Directorate has 3 Regional Offices and 14 District Offices located across the state\r\nCurrently, all functional and administrative activities of the Directorate are carried out manually and are recorded in registers at the respective offices. This data is consolidated at the Directorate for monitoring purposes based on specific requirement. The process of collection and compiling of data from the various offices is time consuming and error prone, which affects the overall efficiency of the organization.”','The Campus Area Network and Enterprise Software (CANES) project involved the implementation of a Network Backbone for the institute on Optic Fibre Cable (OFC) connecting the various buildings in the campus. As part of the project Switched Local Area Networks (LANs) were established in each building that were then hooked onto the OFC Network Backbone. The computers in the various sections / departments were then connected to the LAN, establishing a seamless network of computers across the campus. A suite of Software applications for automating 12 functional and administrative activities in the institute was also developed. These applications were deployed centrally on servers, whereby users could access their respective software modules from anywhere in the network.','Project','0.5971666303041042@-@I&PRD.jpg','A','Software Development',83),(33,'BMEDS FOR BIHAR MEDICAL SERVICES & INFRASTRUCTURE CORPORATION','The Directorate of Factories & Boilers is the statutory authority for implementing statutes meant to improve the Safety, Welfare and Health of factory personnel in the Sate. The department was involved in the activities primarily related with issue & renewal of licenses to factories. It is a tedious task for the inspectors to manually keep track of the licensing procedures. The priority was to build up databases for all activities related to factories & boilers in the state.','BMEDS – Bihar Medical Equipments and Drugs System for BMSICL caters to the automation needs of drug and equipment related planning, procurement, distribution and maintenance.  The key areas covered are drug procurement, quality check and its distribution, equipment procurement, allocation and its maintenance. The payments to the suppliers are also managed through this system.','Project','0.7222348506291388@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',84),(34,'QUEST FOR VIKRAM SARABHAI SPACE CENTRE','KERAFED is a co-operative organization under the Government of Kerala engaged in the business of producing and marketing coconut oil. Kerafed had a computerized financial accounting package. This solution was developed on Power Builder 5.0 and the database was on Integra Version 4.0. The operating system used was SCO Unix Version 3.1. The database Integra had many disadvantages. It was relatively slow, lacked trained manpower, support was not available on time, and RDBMS engine was not flexible enough.','QUEST is a software for the structured archival of Non Destructive Testing (NDT) data. The solution, Quest, converts the data / observations / comments etc. of the senior scientists into categorized sections and stores it in a database. It is possible for junior scientists to go through the complete process when he / she is making an inspection in the absence of a senior scientist. The Knowledge based system that was implemented maintains the NDT data for the past 10 years. The software also has the provision for rule based analysis of defect data. In addition to the NDT data the knowledgebase is also capable of storing Radiographic Images, CAD Drawings etc.','Project','0.3717109167286954@-@kerafed.jpg','A','Software Development',85),(35,'UTRN FOR WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION','The Trivandrum Regional Co-operative Milk Producers Union (TRCMPU) is a Kerala government owned organization engaged in the procurement, processing and sale of milk and milk products. A large number of products are produced and marketed by the TRCMPU under the umbrella brand MILMA. The Central Marketing Store is the central distribution point of the organization. Apart from the inventory the store maintains the details of each product sold through the different channels. The Central Marketing Store generates the various reports needed for market analysis by the top management.','The aim of the Universal Trial Reference Number (UTRN) is to facilitate the unique identification of clinical trials submitted to the International Clinical Trials Registry Platform\'s (ICTRP) Search Portal. The software provided facilitated the generation of a unique Universal Trial Reference Number for each of the clinical trials submitted to the International Clinical Trials Registry Platform’s Search Portal. This number aids as an easy reference tool to search a particular trial on a later date.','Project','0.6498021384946787@-@milma.jpg','A','Software Development',86),(36,'HEALTH RESEARCH INFORMATION SYSTEM FOR NIMS','The Directorate of Industries & Commerce is the Govt. department entrusted with the responsibility of providing all assistance to prospective entrepreneurs in the state. Apart from providing all necessary information to the public, the department also assists in the form of providing constructed building space on lease, developed plots, common research facilities, machinery leasing etc. The department helps in financing the ventures of eligible applicants as well. The department has over half a dozen major functional requirements that were currently being done by manual methods. Also, as the department had offices across the state the compilation of information was becoming increasingly difficult.','The Health Research Information System (HRIS), is a repository of information on Research Projects, Publications, Training Programs, Seminars, Workshops and Conferences. The software is a workflow based application, the users from any institution in the country can access and/or update information based on authorization.','Project','0.2903235716388807@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',87),(37,'DATA MIGRATION FOR AG OFFICE, KERALA STATE','The Office of the Accountant General, Kerala State at Thiruvananthapuram manages all accounts related to Government and Government personnel in the state. These responsibilities are administered from Trivandrum and also from the regional offices at Kottayam, Ernakulam, Thrissur and Kozhikode. The organization implemented Voucher Level Computerization a few years ago.','The Voucher Level Computerization (VLC) is implemented in all the 5 locations of the organization. Voucher information relating to all Government transactions are updated on the software. Over the period, the software application had become very slow due to the heavy build-up of data. It was beginning to take a long time to generate even routine reports from the application.','Project','0.6656264371796141@-@gok.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',59),(38,'NATIONAL HEALTH ACCOUNTS FOR MINISTRY OF HEALTH, GOI','The \"Kerala State Beverages (M & M) Corporation\" (KSBC) is a Public Sector Enterprise owned by the Govt. of Kerala and is the sole distributor for Alcoholic Products in the State. KSBC has 14 warehouses across the state from which nearly 250 retail outlets are being serviced. The turnover of the organization is nearly US$ 1 Billion. With a distributed model of buying, stocking and reselling, access to information on demand is a major factor for effective management. Though the organization had put in place an IT infrastructure that provides the top management with macro level information, it was difficult to get micro level information on demand.','NHA is responsible for tracking the Health Resource utilization, analysing health fund distribution across different services, tracking health expenditure trends and making financial projection of national health system requirements. The software solution enables the NHA Cell to generate various reports in short notice. The financial data can to be presented in various formats for analytical and decision making purposes. The software facilitates multiple personnel of the NHA to access and update information simultaneously and also permit others with authorization to generate various reports on demand.','Project','0.6345664391564757@-@ksbc.jpg','A','Software Development',88),(39,'ADMIRE FOR INFORMATION & PUBLIC RELATIONS DEPARTMENT, GOVT. OF KERALA','During the initial phases of computerization the functional areas of the department was automated. At the Directorate, a number of administrative procedures are followed. Moreover the entire data from across the state is consolidated at the Directorate. In this phase it was decided that the administrative areas at the Directorate be automated. The solution was to develop a Personnel Information and Management System for the Directorate. The solution was expected to aid in automating various administrative areas of the Directorate. It was to be a basket of software applications including personnel information system, file management system, payroll and transfers & postings. Effective utilization of IT in the core administrative areas was expected to result in significant improvements in efficiency, and reduction of workload in the Directorate.','It is an online platform for the I&PRD Dept. that helps to manage the advertisements and it comprises of functions like Advertisement Request Submission, Verification and Processing by the organization, Issue of Release Orders, Order Acceptance and Bill Submission by Media, Submission of Bills by Media, Payment Processing by the organization etc. The software maintains the details of each media house including geographical circulation/ coverage, category etc. The release of orders can also be systematically managed through AdMIRe.','Project','0.0059894918826693955@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',89),(40,'DATABASE MIGRATION OF FINANCIAL ACCOUNTING SOLUTION – KERAFED','The Kerala State Industrial Infrastructure Corporation Ltd. (Kinfra), a Government of Kerala Undertaking, is in the business of developing industrial estates in different parts of the state to lease out to industrial units. Kinfra has currently set up 11 industrial parks in various parts of the state catering to multiple industrial sectors with new parks being added on a regular basis. After procuring large tracts of land, Kinfra develops the same as suitable for specific industrial purposes and sells / leases it out to industrial units. An industrial unit can either buy the land/shed or lease it on long-term basis.\r\n\r\nKinfra manages a large number of applicants for Plots / Sheds and keeps track of the repayment of existing units. As the process of allotment and repayment are different for each park and for each industry sector, it is very difficult to ensure the correctness of the process consistently. Also the workload increases with the addition of each new park.\r\n','To overcome the disadvantages that persisted with the existing software it was found necessary to migrate to Oracle RDBMS. The operating system was changed to Windows NT, keeping pace with the changes in technology. The front end for the software was reworked using Developer 2000. The software aids in migrating the existing software application module on Integra / UNIX to Oracle / NT. The application was designed on Developer 2000 with Oracle as its backend. The design and creation of tables in Oracle was done to facilitate smooth data transfer from the existing Integra database. The software is more user friendly as well as the transaction speeds are higher.','Project','0.3472947517974838@-@kinfra.jpg','A','Software Development',90),(41,'ALLOTMENT & REPAYMENT MONITORING SOLUTION, KINFRA','The Kerala State Industrial Infrastructure Corporation Ltd. (Kinfra), a Government of Kerala Undertaking, is in the business of developing industrial estates in different parts of the state to lease out to industrial units. Kinfra has currently set up 11 industrial parks in various parts of the state catering to multiple industrial sectors with new parks being added on a regular basis. After procuring large tracts of land, Kinfra develops the same as suitable for specific industrial purposes and sells / leases it out to industrial units. An industrial unit can either buy the land/shed or lease it on long-term basis.\r\n\r\nKinfra manages a large number of applicants for Plots / Sheds and keeps track of the repayment of existing units. As the process of allotment and repayment are different for each park and for each industry sector, it is very difficult to ensure the correctness of the process consistently. Also the workload increases with the addition of each new park.','A software solution for Repayment and Allotment Monitoring was recommended following a detailed study at Kinfra. The software solution, ARAM, is designed to keep track of the applicants to various units in each park and ensure the compliance of all formalities before a unit is allocated to an applicant. ARAM also manages the periodic repayments by the various units in the different parks. The software solution generates the monthly repayment schedule for each unit based on the approved interest rate for the park / industry sector','Project','0.30288131962869336@-@kinfra.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',60),(42,'MARKETING STORE MANAGEMENT SOFTWARE FOR KERALA CO-OPERATIVE MILK MARKETING FEDERATION','Kerala Medical Services Corporation Limited (KMSCL) is a fully owned Government of Kerala company set up in 2007 for providing services to various health care institutions under Department of Family Welfare and Health. One of the key objectives of the KMSCL is to act as the central procurement agency for all essential drugs and equipments for all public healthcare institutions (hereinafter referred to as user institutions) under the department. The company is procuring drugs worth more than Rs.170 Crores & above 250 different types of medical equipments and also provides essential services needed for health sector. It has also been mandated with the setting up and running of all kinds of modem Medical and Paramedical or medical based ancillary facilities such as hospitals, pathological labs, diagnostic centers, x-ray/scanning facilities. The Government of Kerala formulated KMSCL.\r\n\r\nIt is proposed to implement a comprehensive solution covering the core functional as well as administrative areas of the organization.','The software solution implemented consists of three major modules namely Product Inventory, Sales and Marketing. Product inventory takes care of inventory management and is integrated to Sales module. It generates consolidated reports of inventory position on a daily basis. The Sales Application handles the sales through various channels. All the cash transactions related to sales are maintained in the software. The Marketing Information System aids the management in taking useful decisions by analysing the various aspects of sales.','Project','0.7358448848346085@-@kmscl.jpg','A','Software Development',91),(43,'TASK” FOR KERALA MEDICAL SERVICES CORPORATION','Kerala Medical Services Corporation Limited (KMSCL) is a fully owned Government of Kerala company set up in 2007 for providing services to various health care institutions under Department of Family Welfare and Health. One of the key objectives of the KMSCL is to act as the central procurement agency for all essential drugs and equipments for all public healthcare institutions (hereinafter referred to as user institutions) under the department. The company is procuring drugs worth more than Rs.170 Crores & above 250 different types of medical equipments and also provides essential services needed for health sector. It has also been mandated with the setting up and running of all kinds of modem Medical and Paramedical or medical based ancillary facilities such as hospitals, pathological labs, diagnostic centers, x-ray/scanning facilities. The Government of Kerala formulated KMSCL.\r\n\r\nIt is proposed to implement a comprehensive solution covering the core functional as well as administrative areas of the organization.','TASK – Total Automation Solution for KMSCL is a web based solution built on open technologies that caters to the total automation needs of the organization. The solution is work flow enabled wherein users will have different roles and responsibilities. The key areas covered are drug procurement, quality check and its distribution, equipment procurement, allocation and its maintenance, HR management, file management, asset management, financial accounting.','Project','0.8896719831840683@-@kmscl.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',61),(44,'AMBER FOR KERALA STATE BEVERAGES CORPORATION','Kerala Road Transport Corporation (K S R T C) was established by the Government of Kerala in 1965.  K S R T C is the only public transport system that caters to the road transport needs of the people of the state. The corporation has a fleet strength of 4704 Nos. comprising of 2940 Leyland, 1562 Tata, 200 Eicher and 2 Volvos. Out of these 2124 buses (45.15%) are aged more than 7 years of life. Apart from the state wide service inter state buses are also operated by the Corporation. In order to leverage the benefits of information technology the Corporation aims at automating the key functional as well as administrative areas.','Data from the Billing Machines at the retail outlets are uploaded to the server at the respective warehouses. This data is consolidated at the warehouse and various reports are generated for the warehouse managers. The consolidated data from the warehouse is again transferred to the Central Server at the Head Office. The requisite reports are generated from the consolidated data from all warehouses of the organization. This information is made available to all the authorized personnel at the HO. The software has two versions, for the head office and the warehouse, respectively. The Head Office application is mainly for consolidation of data sent from the warehouses. The data received from the warehouses will include the details of transactions of each retail outlet collected through the electronic billing machine. The solution at the warehouse is for consolidation of the data from the electronic billing machines at the retail outlets.','Project','0.6941105077112004@-@ksrtc.jpg','A','Software Development',92),(45,'SAARATHI“ FOR KERALA STATE  ROAD TRANSPORT CORPORATION','Kerala Road Transport Corporation (K S R T C) was established by the Government of Kerala in 1965.  K S R T C is the only public transport system that caters to the road transport needs of the people of the state. The corporation has a fleet strength of 4704 Nos. comprising of 2940 Leyland, 1562 Tata, 200 Eicher and 2 Volvos. Out of these 2124 buses (45.15%) are aged more than 7 years of life. Apart from the state wide service inter state buses are also operated by the Corporation. In order to leverage the benefits of information technology the Corporation aims at automating the key functional as well as administrative areas.','The current proposal is to develop a suite of over 50 interdependent applications to automate the core administrative as well as functional areas of the organization so that the organization can be effectively managed as a compact entity. The major software applications suites are for Fleet Management, Revenue Management, Schedule Management and various other administrative functions. Also covered are Financial Accounting and corporate Intranet solution. Routine reports would be generated automatically from the respective software modules. The solution envisages the total computerisation of the organisation.','Project','0.4135134076597816@-@ksrtc.jpg','A','Maintenance & Support',62),(46,'ARAM FOR KERALA INDUSTRIAL INFRASTRUCTURE DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION','The Department of Tourism is headed by the Director.  It has three major functions such as (i) Tourism Development in State (ii) Providing hospitality services to the State Government and (iii) Estate Office duty. The Department provides accommodation and transport to the State Guests for which, it maintains 24 guesthouses across the country. As part of Tourism Development, new destinations are being identified and various schemes are being implemented to develop them as important tourist spots in the State. Department is providing assistance to District Tourism Promotion Councils (DTPCs) in all the districts. For improving the efficiency of the organization by leveraging on the benefits of information technology the Directorate aims at automating the monitoring of various projects underway at various locations of the state. ','A software solution for Repayment and Allotment Monitoring was developed and implemented following a detailed study at Kinfra. The software solution, ARAM, is designed to keep track of the applicants to various units in each park and ensure the compliance of all formalities before a unit is allocated to an applicant. ARAM also manages the periodic repayments by the various units in the different parks. The software solution generates the monthly repayment schedule for each unit based on the approved interest rate for the park / industry sector.','Project','0.5800556111700695@-@krala tourism.jpg','A','Software Development',93),(47,'TOTAL AUTOMATION FOR KURIAN ABRAHAM LTD','The Department of Tourism is headed by the Director.  It has three major functions such as (i) Tourism Development in State (ii) Providing hospitality services to the State Government and (iii) Estate Office duty. The Department provides accommodation and transport to the State Guests for which, it maintains 24 guesthouses across the country. As part of Tourism Development, new destinations are being identified and various schemes are being implemented to develop them as important tourist spots in the State. Department is providing assistance to District Tourism Promotion Councils (DTPCs) in all the districts. For improving the efficiency of the organization by leveraging on the benefits of information technology the Directorate aims at automating the monitoring of various projects underway at various locations of the state.','Based on the requirements analysis conducted, an IT solution was proposed that involved setting up of a private network connecting all the locations to the Head Office and generating various marketing related reports. The solution proposed facilitates the respective users in the Marketing Department with information on Sales, Order Status, Order Processing and a wide range of reports. The information pertaining to marketing activities right from the receipt of an enquiry to the point of product dispatch can be maintained in the system. A wide range of parameterized reports can be generated from the system.','Project','0.5583683605163343@-@ka.jpg','A','Consultancy',52),(48,'TASK FOR KERALA MEDICAL SERVICES CORPORATION','The Commissionerate of Police (CoP)– Kochi City, Kerala State, has on its rolls over 3000 Police Personnel at various levels and a vehicle fleet numbering over 250. The CoP has nearly 20 sub offices and a central administrative office manned by around 60 administrative staff.  All administrative activities of CoP – Kochi City were managed through manual systems. This includes Personnel Administration, Financial Administration, Fleet Administration etc. \r\n\r\nDue to the very high volume of work, the time taken for generating routine reports was very high and often the reports were not accurate. This also had an adverse impact on personnel morale as Leave applications; Loan applications etc. were not processed on time.','TASK – Total Automation Solution for KMSCL is a web based solution built on open technologies that caters to the total automation needs of the organization. The solution is work flow enabled wherein users will have different roles and responsibilities. The key areas covered are drug procurement, quality check and its distribution, equipment procurement, allocation and its maintenance, HR management, file management, asset management, financial accounting.','Project','0.3616722558813502@-@police.jpg','A','Software Development',94),(49,'SAARATHI FOR KERALA STATE ROAD TRANSPORT CORPORATION','KPHCC is engaged in the business of civil construction and maintenance. KPHCC takes up assignments across the state, from Kerala Police Department and from Kerala Government. The corporation has its head office in Trivandrum and project engineers manage the construction activities in the various districts. \r\n\r\nKPHCC executes the various projects assigned to it, by subcontracting to specialised agencies. For this, Tenders are invited for undertaking specific works as per an approved design and schedule.  Work orders are issued from KPHCC HO in Trivandrum, to contractors who meet the minimum criteria and quote the lowest charges.\r\n\r\nThe core function of order and payment processing was fully managed through manual systems. Considering the volume of work, the time taken for processing an order and effecting the payment is a time consuming clerical work. It was therefore proposed to implement an automated solution for streamlining the work order generation and payment processing','Saarathi is a suite of over 50 interdependent applications to automate the core administrative as well as functional areas of the organization so that the organization can be effectively managed as a compact entity. The major software applications suites are for Fleet Management, Revenue Management, Schedule Management and various other administrative functions. Also covered are Financial Accounting and corporate Intranet solution. Routine reports would be generated automatically from the respective software modules.','Project','0.2253120292812869@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',95),(50,'E-ADMIN FOR FEDERATION OF INDIAN EXPORT ORGANIZATIONS','The State Police Headquarters of Kerala has the overall administrative responsibility of the entire police establishment in the state. The Kerala PHQ has over 500 sub offices and a central administrative office manned by around 200 administrative staff.  All administrative activities of Kerala PHQ were managed through manual systems. This includes Personnel Administration, Financial Administration, Legal Issue Administration etc. The department employs over 30,000 personnel at various levels and as a result the administrative sections of the PHQ have their hands full with routine administrative work.\r\n\r\nBecause of the unique nature of the department, it is often necessary to generate accurate reports within a very short time frame. Due to the very high volume of work, this is not always possible and leads to delay in decision-making. As the decision at the PHQ has a cascading effect down to the district offices, this has an adverse impact on the overall efficiency of the department.','The project is an ERP class custom built suite of applications to automate the core administrative as well as functional areas of the organization. The solution includes functional modules for Registration cum Membership of Exporters, Trade & Tender Enquiries and Exporter’s Problem Management System. It also covers administrative modules for HR, File Processing & Tracking Solution and Intranet Software.','Project','0.2393192610277345@-@police.jpg','A','Software Development',96),(51,'SMART OFFICE FOR COMMISSIONERATE OF POLICE- KOCHI CITY','The Crime Branch Department of Kerala Police investigates around 1000 cases on an average every year. The department has special investigating units spread across the state. Based on the nature and geographic location of each case, a unit is allocated the task of investigation of a case by the Headquarters of the department. Each case is investigated by an exclusive team, which meticulously documents all relevant information about the case. The investigation process of many of these cases is lengthy, as data collection and information gathering is laborious and time consuming. \r\n\r\nAn elaborate manual system of reporting is in place through which the status of a case at the field level is reported to the headquarters. In spite of this, due to the high workload, and number of cases, it is often difficult for the senior officers at the Department Headquarters to know the current status of a particular case. Getting information as and when needed is difficult due to the inherent drawbacks of a manual system. Also, it is difficult to crosscheck the authenticity and accuracy of the collected information.','A detailed study was conducted at the Commissionerate of Police – Kochi City to identify the routine and repetitive tasks carried out by the administrative sections in the office. Based on the study 20 areas amenable to computerisation were identified. SmartOffice, a suite of software applications, was developed specifically catering to each of the identified areas. SmartOffice comprises of 20 Software modules that are interdependent and fully integrated. The process of implementation of the various software modules of SmartOffice at site is currently on. The implementation involves setting up the software, updating the software with the necessary back data, providing end user training and hand holding support.','Project','0.27824114412104706@-@police.jpg','A','Software Development',97),(52,'ARCHIVE MANAGEMENT AT AG’S OFFICE, KERALA STATE','Office of the Accountant General at Thiruvananthapuram has 5 major departments dealing with Pension, Provident Fund, Gazetted Entitlement, Accounts and General Administration. All the accounts related to Government and Government personnel are maintained at the AG’s office. The Provident Fund and Pension Details of all Government Staff are handled at this office.  The AG’s Office at Thiruvananthapuram generates nearly 100,000 files every year of which almost 50 per cent are Pension related. \r\n\r\nWhile the files that are currently being processed are kept in the respective sections, the closed files are moved to the archives. These files are kept in the Archives Section for varying periods according to the nature of the file. The archived files are retrieved only if they are required at a later point of time for reference purposes. All information pertaining to Archiving and Retrieving of closed Files is maintained in various registers in the Archives Section. Over the years, a huge number of files have accumulated in the Archive Section, making it very difficult to locate a file. Due to the physical nature of storage it is also practically impossible to identify files that are to be disposed off based on a specified time period leading to further accumulation of files.','A detailed study was conducted and a software solution was proposed to keep track of the Closed Files, Indexing Details, Re-issue details and Final Disposal. The proposed solution would have specific modules for Indexing, Transfer to Archives, Registration at Archive, Requisition for Referencing, and Transfer to Section & Back to Archive, Permanent Disposal and Reports. Users can search and submit requisition for retrieval of files for referencing.','Project','0.15564003984356956@-@krala tourism.jpg','A','Consultancy',53),(53,'ORDER AND PAYMENT PROCESSING SOLUTION, KERALA POLICE HOUSING CONSTRUCTION CORPORATION','NORKA - ROOTS, an establishment of Government of Kerala is an agency set up to take care of the welfare of the Non-Resident Keralites. The organization is headquartered in Trivandrum and has presence in major cities in Kerala. Apart from managing the welfare schemes initiated by the state government for the non-resident Keralites (NRKs) as a group, the organization also takes up projects in association with individual NRKs.  NORKA – ROOTS, having been recently formed, is in the process of implementing systems and procedures for streamlining internal processes and project administration.   \r\n\r\nThe absence of legacy systems and procedures provided an opportunity to implement systematically devised IT based systems and procedures so that the service to the target clientele is effectively delivered. ','The solution aids in the automation of the major functional activities of the Police Housing Corporation right from the acceptance of a project through the preparation of drawings and schedules, tendering, monitoring and effecting payments. The software application consists of various modules like Processing of Orders, E-Tendering (Comprise sub modules like Vendor Registration, Tender Notification, Bid Submission, Bid Comparison & Vendor History), Issuing Work Orders, Progress Monitoring, M-Book Management (M-Book Preparation & M-Book Verification), Bill Preparation & Bill Processing. Once deployed the solution aids in streamlining the work order generation and payment processing activities of the organization.','Project','0.19115074007967547@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',98),(54,'OFFICE AUTOMATION SOLUTION FOR KERALA POLICE HEADQUARTERS','Asianet Cable Vision (ACV) has its head office located at Thiruvananthapuram. Apart from the HO, the organisation has 36 centres across the state.  Most of the centres are locally managed by Video Service Providers (VSP). A major part of ACV’s revenue comes from commercial advertisements. The Marketing team prepares a commercial proposal after checking out the availability of the requested time slot, based on a client enquiry. On receipt of the Release Order from the client, the Marketing team generates an internal Release Order for the Studio detailing the relevant particulars as requested by the client. Once the advertisement is aired a Telecast Confirmation Certificate (TCC) is generated and the corresponding invoice is prepared. \r\n\r\nAs the process involves close co-ordination and sharing of information between the Marketing section, Studio and Accounts Departments, various registers are required to be maintained. These registers need to be updated regularly so that right information is available to the right person on time. Each register entails duplicating information adding to workload of the personnel. ','A detailed study conducted at the Kerala State Police Headquarters identified 20 areas amenable for computerisation in the administrative sections of the office. The study at the PHQ was done based on the earlier study conducted at the District Office of the department (CoP – Kochi). SmartOffice, a suite of software applications was developed specifically catering to each of the identified areas. SmartOffice comprises of 20 Software modules that are interdependent and fully integrated. SmartOffice for PHQ also envisages the requirement of integrating and consolidation of information from the various district offices of the department. The process of implementation of the various software modules of SmartOffice at site is currently on. The implementation involves setting up the software, updating the software with the necessary back data, providing end user training and hand holding support.','Project','0.0865534584056199@-@asianet.jpg','A','Software Development',99),(55,'CRIME INVESTIGATION MANAGEMENT FOR KERALA POLICE','Various routine activities like Admission Management, Fee Collection, School Bus Management, Time Table preparation, Mark List Tabulation etc. were identified, where automation could play a major part to improve efficiency. \r\n\r\nApart from the administration process, due to the stringent procedures adopted by monitoring agencies, various mandatory reports are to be filed with the respective agencies on a periodic basis. This also takes up a lot of time of the administration staff.\r\n','A software solution designed to monitor the progress of investigation was developed and deployed for the Crime Branch Department. The solution put in place a reporting mechanism by which the investigative officers were able update the status of cases handled by them. The software solution is hosted on a Central Server on an Intranet and is accessible to all users in the network. Based on authorisation, users can access or modify the data. Data submitted by the concerned person is automatically available to the next superior officer for approval. The Crime Branch Headquarters can generate various reports to monitor the progress of investigation at each Investigating unit in the state. Reports can also be generated of the progress on each case and also the complete investigation details of the individual case.','Project','0.7289679705532766@-@lds.jpg','A','Software Development',100),(56,'OFFICE AUTOMATION FOR NORKA-ROOTS, GOVERNMENT OF KERALA','The number of cases registered by the Kerala Police Department involving Vehicle Theft is very high. The registration and follow-up of such cases are done across the state in the various offices of the department. The registration of each vehicle theft case involves updating many registers. Details being maintained in each case includes the Complainant Details, Owner Details, Device Details, Extra Fittings etc., Accused Details, Description of Vehicle, Receiver of Property, Recovery Details, Gang Details like Members Involved, Operational Areas, Cases Involved, Associate Details, Agent Details etc. Due to the voluminous increase in the number of cases it has become difficult to manage the records manually. \r\n\r\nThe manual system of maintaining registers has the drawback that information cannot be shared as and when needed with other offices under the department leading to a delay in responding adequately to apprehend the culprit.','The implemented solution comprises of a suite of software applications, which automates the core administrative and functional operations of the organization. This ensures that the organization is effectively administered as a compact entity. The software modules implemented at NORKA – ROOTS as part of the current project are 1) Attendance Management, 2) Payroll 3) Financial Accounting 4) Asset Register 5) Visitors’ Register 6) Entrepreneurship Development and 7) File Tracking & Processing Solution. All routine reports that were being generated manually are now generated automatically from the respective software modules.','Project','0.753400978272403@-@police.jpg','A','Software Development',101),(57,'VEHICLE THEFT INFORMATION SYSTEM FOR KERALA POLICE','The Commissionerate of Entrance Examinations (CEE) is the sole agency set up by Government of Kerala to conduct Entrance Examinations for  admission to various professional courses offered in Government and Private colleges in the state. The Commissionerate of Entrance Examinations conducts a joint Entrance Examination every year for admission to professional courses like Engineering, Medicine, Agriculture, Veterinary etc. Over 50,000 candidates appear for the examination to secure a Course and College of his / her choice. Based on the common rank list the Commissionerate gives admission to the various seats in the colleges. \r\n\r\nConsidering the large number of courses and colleges, and the complex reservation criteria (there are over 25 professional courses in over 50 colleges, and  42 reservation categories having different priorities) makes the admission process cumbersome and long drawn out. Because of the complex nature and the manual involvement in the process there is a possibility of errors creeping in, often leading to litigation.','The Vehicle Theft Information System (VeTIS) was conceived to address this problem. The software maintains the complete details as in manual registers and allows the users to search online for any specific information. The software can be deployed in a Central Server ensuring that any office under the department has access to the database at any point of time. There is no duplication of data entry. Data entered at only place is available to all authorised users across the state. The software also has the facility to maintain photographs, Finger prints and physical features of the Gang members. The physical features covers the nature or structure of body parts like Hair, Nose, Ear, Face, Teeth, and Eyes etc. Various reports can be generated from the software freeing the staff from such mundane duties.','Project','0.40147464398371435@-@police.jpg','A','Software Development',102),(58,'SCHEME/ BENEFIT MANAGEMENT SOLUTION FOR SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY DEPT., GOVT. OF ODISHA','The Office of the Chief Electoral Officer, (CEO) Govt. of Kerala maintains the database of electors in the state. The office has a continuous process of enrolling new voters, removing those who have moved to another location or are deceased. The office has 14 sub offices in each of the districts in the state. The eligible number of electors in the state exceeds 25 Million. The office of the Chief Electoral Officer maintains the database of the eligible electors containing the Name, Age, Address, Photograph etc. Considering the very large number of electors being added, removed, transferred etc. maintaining this database is a very complex process. However the entire process is eminently amenable for computerisation.','The solution is primarily focused on automating the process flow related to the various schemes and benefits offered by the Science & Technology department. The solution facilitates online registration of beneficiaries – individual, institution and organizations, work flow automation of scheme / benefit management with request processing. It also includes mobile apps for registration, inspection and querying. A comprehensive web portal for the department is also designed for facilitating information dissemination to both internal as well as external stakeholders. Various informative reports and dashboard are also included as part of the solution.','Project','0.011305082313506354@-@police.jpg','A','Software Development',103),(59,'CAMS FOR CONTROLLER OF ENTRANCE EXAMS, GOVERNMENT OF KERALA','Kerala Khadi and Village Industries Board (KVIB), is an organization set up by Government of Kerala.  The primary focus of the organisation is in the development of small-scale industries and cottage industries amongst the traditional sector in the state. The organization assists the entrepreneurs to source, manufacture and sell their goods collectively. It also provides them with financial assistance and skill upgradation schemes. KVIB has offices, showrooms and warehouses in various parts of the state. \r\n\r\nAll financial transactions and report generation in KVIB was through manual processes. As the volume of transactions increased there was a need to automate the processes that are amenable to computerisation in the finance department of the organization.','The software solution Common Admission Management System (CAMS), streamlined the process of admission management. The solution automates the process of determining the eligibility for admission based on conditions like rank for the relevant stream, minimum marks for the qualifying exam, age, reservation eligibility, selected course and selected college. As the system eliminates human intervention completely, the admission process became totally transparent leading to better confidence in the system and reducing litigation. The software also facilitated the process of multi-site admissions thereby shortening drastically the time taken for completing the whole admission process.','Project','0.6066220840487614@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',104),(60,'ProbityFinancials','Integrated Financial Management System','It is an Integrated Financial Management System for any state,  providing single source of Truth about the State Finance. It helps the states to achieve prudent Fiscal Management with fair projection of Monthly Expenditure and Receipts, details of Current Liabilities, details of department wise, office wise Expenditure & Receipts, its Projections and Tracking all office wise Commitments. It handles the various aspects of State Finance like Projections, Transactions, Revisions, Monitoring and Reporting. It can be integrated with relevant financial information pertaining to DDOs, HoDs, Departments, Treasury, Banks, RBI and AG. ','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',27),(61,'Outcome Budget','','An outcome-based Budgeting approach shifts the perspective from mere allocation of funds to the short and long-term outcomes of governance.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',28),(62,'Sectoral Budget','','To make Budget more inclusive, provision to specify budgeting components like Child/ Girl Child, Divyang, Elderly etc. while submitting expenditure.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',29),(63,'Debt Management','','To ensure that the government\'s financing needs and its payment obligations are met at the lowest possible cost over the medium to long run, consistent with a prudent degree of risk.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',30),(64,'RIDF-NABARD','','Solution to Monitor Rural Infrastructure Development funds of NABARD through State Government.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',31),(65,'NPS-NSDL','','To provide hassle-free National Pension System (NPS) registration experience to government employees.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',32),(66,'ProMIS','Project Monitoring System','It is a project monitoring solution that aids in maintaining the details of all projects undertaken by an organization like general details, cost details, funding details, funds received, schedules & milestones tracking, progress tracking, utilization etc.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',33),(67,'ReMIS','Report Monitoring System ','It is a solution designed for monitoring reports, prepared on the basis of audit conducted at various union and state government departments which includes sub modules like CAG reports, inspection reports & policy recommendations.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',34),(68,'AIMS','Audit Management System','Audit Information Management System “AIMS” is an end-to-end platform for managing the complete audit life cycle of government auditing agencies to make it more effective and meaningful. It covers the audit related activities of the organization right from the receipt of annual financial statements through audit calendar preparation, team formation, recording audit observations, generation of audit report and tracking to its closure.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',35),(69,'IMS','Inspection Management System','Inspection Management System “IMS”, is a solution for any department / organization that conducts detailed inspection eventually resulting in inspection reports and action taken reports. It helps in automation of inspection related information such as registration of complaints, scheduling inspections, recording results and observations, recommending corrective measures, track corrective actions to closure thus strengthening the Inspection Process.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',36),(70,'CharMS','Charitable Endowments','Charitable endowments Management System “CharMS” is a web based solution for the Management and Monitoring of Charitable Endowments of various Organizations / Establishments/ Persons by the state government.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',37),(71,'Panchayat Financials','','','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',38),(72,'Sirius','Macro Fiscal Projection','It is a solution for the preparation of “Macro Fiscal Projection”, for a state which includes collection, validation, consolidation of primary and secondary data from external sources for the projection & generation of macro fiscal projection. Sector wise forms are available for the capture of survey data and in turn this data forms the basis for Macro Fiscal Projection.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',39),(73,'Village Index Register','','Village Index Register is a annually Organized, maintained and consolidated statistical data of a village.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',40),(74,'MFP','Macro Fiscal Projection','Data Consolidation And Projection with regard to the various surveys and data collection as part of the functional activity of the directorate of economics and statistics of the state.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',41),(75,'SSFC','Solution for State Finance Commission','A web portal for the State Finance Commission, to collect, consolidate requisite data from the Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRI) and Urban Local Bodies (UBI) and to generate various reports.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',42),(76,'Orion','Loan Management System','It is a comprehensive Loan Management System that covers activities right from loan application, through scrutiny, processing and sanction, disbursement, repayment monitoring etc. to its closure. It aids in the maintenance of beneficiary database thereby\r\nensuring effective monitoring of financial inclusion reaching out to a wider spectrum.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',43),(77,'Optimus','Fund & Benefit Management System','It is a Fund & Benefit Management System which can be effectively utilized as a digital platform for Direct Benefit Transfer to the eligible beneficiaries. It helps in the quick release of financial assistance to any category of the society like Construction Workers, Migrant Workers, Agricultural Workers, Students stuck abroad etc., with an interface to Banking Gateway.','Product',NULL,'A','Public Finance',44),(78,'DBT','Direct Beneficiary Transfer','Transfer the subsidies of various social welfare schemes directly to the bank account of the beneficiaries. In-between leakages and inordinate delays will be avoided, and ensures the most appropriate people are benefited.','Product',NULL,'D','Public Finance',45),(79,'SDG - Mapping','','A module that facilitate preparation of outcome based budget and linking financial estimates with outcomes related to Sustainable Development Goals','Project',NULL,'A','Public Finance',66),(80,'Phoenix','e-Regulation System','It is an e-Regulation software for any organization that is regulatory in nature. It helps in the automation of issuing license / permit, renewal of license, amendment of license, transfer of license, generation of duplicate license etc. The solution facilitates the integration with e-payment, SMS / Email gateways etc. For authentication of license / permit documents,','Product',NULL,'A','Permits, Licensing & Compliance',25),(81,'Helix','Welfare Management Solution','This solution aids in the registration, subscription, processing of welfare benefits as per set norms, beneficiary management, corpus fund management etc. It can be utilized by the welfare boards of different sectors.','Product',NULL,'A','Permits, Licensing & Compliance',26),(82,'Stage','File Management System','Stage is a software solution for Speedy and Transparent Processing of Files in government establishments. It is a complete file processing system starting from the inward registration to file creation, file noting, file tracking, issue of correspondence till file archiving as per the Whitehall method of filing. Any organization can be rapidly brought within the STAGE framework without impairing the existing processes during migration. STAGE could be the first major step towards comprehensive electronic processing of files in any government organization.','Product',NULL,'A','General Administration',8),(83,'Edge','HR Management System','It is a HR management solution that keeps track of all the details of an employee right from appointment to cessation of service. It automates the key HR functions like employee service book, leave, paybill / payroll etc. A self-service facility is available for the employees to view real time information regarding their service book, leave, pay etc. It helps in the generation of a comprehensive employee profile on a real time basis. ','Product',NULL,'A','General Administration',9),(84,'GAdmin','General Administration Management System','GAdmin is a comprehensive solution that helps manage the information pertaining to different resources/facilities of an organization. It is a suite of software solutions for managing the routine general administrative functions of an organization. Once implemented it is an easy monitoring tool and acts as an effective decision support mechanism for the administrators. It consists of seven base modules namely Purchase & Inventory, Asset, Stationery, Vehicle, Resource, Project, Utility etc.','Product',NULL,'A','General Administration',13),(85,'Galaxy','ERP Class Solution for Administrative Areas of PSUs','It is an ERP class solution that covers all administrative areas of a typical Public Sector Unit. It covers various administrative areas like file processing, human resource management, intra-organizational communication suite, financial accounting based on double entry system. It also has a general administration module that comprise of sub modules related to routine administrative needs of an organization.','Product',NULL,'A','Enterprise Resource Planning',3),(86,'GalaxyALMS','Application Life Cycle Management System','It is a fully integrated application for monitoring software development life cycle. This is an end to end project monitoring solution that helps in managing the software projects right from planning stage to its execution. It is an effective tool that helps in proper estimation, schedule compliance, resource optimization etc. It also aids in the monitoring and control throughout the development life cycle.','Product',NULL,'A','Enterprise Resource Planning',4),(87,'GalaxyMED','Integrated Solution for Medical Services Corporations','It is a fully integrated application for monitoring software development life cycle. This is an end to end project monitoring solution that helps in managing the software projects right from planning stage to its execution. It is an effective tool that helps in proper estimation, schedule compliance, resource optimization etc. It also aids in the monitoring and control throughout the development life cycle.','Product',NULL,'A','Enterprise Resource Planning',5),(88,'Saarathi','ERP Class Solution for Road Transport Corporation','It is an ERP class solution for transport corporations that aids in the automation of core functional, administrative, financial and managerial information. The key modules include online ticketing, fleet management, route management, fare structure management, HR management, general administration and dashboard based MIS. Once implemented, the organization can be effectively managed as a compact entity.','Product',NULL,'A','Enterprise Resource Planning',2),(89,'SmartOffice','ERP Class Solution for Administrative Areas of Govt. Depts','It is an ERP class solution that covers all administrative areas of a typical government department. It covers various administrative areas like file processing, human resource management, intra-departmental communication suite, financial accounting based on single entry system. It also has a general administration module that comprise of sub modules related to routine administrative needs of a department.','Product',NULL,'A','Enterprise Resource Planning',1),(90,'SmartWings','Integrated Office Automation System','It is a solution for office automation that comprises of two software products STAGE and SmartNet customized for defense units. STAGE can be used for processing of files and SmartNet can be used for intraoffice communication between the users.','Product',NULL,'D','Enterprise Resource Planning',6),(91,'SmartWorks','Public Works Management System','It is an end to end solution that aids in automating the “Works Management” of Public Works Department which includes facilities like project initiation, sanctions, contract ?nalization, work progress monitoring, M-book entry, billing & its closure.','Product',NULL,'D','Enterprise Resource Planning',7),(92,'SmartNet','Intra-Organization Communication System','SmartNet is an intra-organizational communication and collaboration suite that invariably serves as an efficient tool for easy communication among the employees of an organization. The features of SmartNet comprise of meetings, notifications, greetings, discussion forum, directory, diary, messaging, holiday listing etc. SmartNet is designed to be the primary mode of communication between the employees in the organization. Facility is provided for the user to send inter department or intra office notes. The solution can be integrated with other administrative and functional modules viz. payroll, leave management etc.','Product',NULL,'A','General Administration',12),(93,'eMetier','Online Employment Portal','It is a web based job portal system which can be used by job seekers to submit their CV and apply for jobs. On the other hand potential employers can select best employees from available CV database based on their requirements. The system includes facilities like candidate registration & profiles, job search, employer registration & profiles etc.','Product',NULL,'A','Others',20),(94,'Orbit','Supply Chain Management System','It is a supply chain solution that aids in the automation of processes pertaining to centralized procurement, inventory control and distribution of any product. The key features include indent preparation, consolidation and its finalization, tender process management, purchase process management, stock management, distribution etc. It also helps in the generation of demand forecasting.','Product',NULL,'A','Others',21),(95,'Indenture','Order & Payment Processing System','It is a solution for automating the core functional activities of any Public Construction Corporation, right from processing of requests for construction through capture of feasibility study report, attachment of drawings & schedules, preparation of estimates, tender & order processing, progress monitoring, bill & payment processing to its closure.','Product',NULL,'A','Others',22),(96,'Edify','Training Administration System','It is a training management solution for any training institute/ training wing of any department that conducts scheduled training throughout the year. It is an effective tool for the training administrators which aids in the effective planning and utilization of available resources, conducting training programs or scheduled short term and long term courses based on a pre-defined calendar.','Product',NULL,'A','Others',19),(97,'ARAM','Allotment and Repayment Management','A solution to automate the Land / Building Allotment process in any industry park. It has multiple modules taking care of the entire process of acquisition of  a suitable land, its development and selling / leasing the same to investors.','Product',NULL,'D','Others',24),(98,'AdMIRe','Advertisement Management System','Advertisement Management Information Repository “AdMIRe” is a solution that automates the routine functions of Information & Public Relations department of a state government related to advertisement management. The broad functions covered are advertisement request, issue of release order, submission of bills, verifications, payment processes etc.','Product',NULL,'A','Others',23),(99,'Probity','Finance Management System','It is a financial accounting system which helps in the automation of major financial functions of a public sector unit based on double entry accounting system. It covers details like receipts, payments, contra entry, journal entry, statutory details, trial balance etc. It helps in the generation various financial statements like cash book, bank book, profit & loss, balance sheet etc.. It is an integrated component of the galaxy suite.','Product',NULL,'A','General Administration',10),(100,'ProbityFMS','Budgeting & Expenditure Monitoring','It is a financial accounting system which helps in the automation of major financial functions of a government department based on single entry accounting system. It covers details like receipts & payments etc. It helps in the generation various financial statements like cash book, bank book, income & expenditure statement etc.. It is an integrated component of the SmartOffice suite.','Product',NULL,'A','General Administration',11),(101,'SmartMessenger','SMS Broadcast & Management Platform','This is a platform for SMS Broadcast & Management interfaced with SMS gateway. It covers Message Composing, Bulk Upload of Recipient Numbers, Option to Choose Service Provider, Message Broadcasting, Archive of Broadcasted Messages, E-Mail Integration and Dashboard Summary of Activities','Product',NULL,'D','Others',18),(102,'Vet. Cares','Culling Management System','It is an online culling management system that captures data of affected livestock and facilitates the processing of compensation to the eligible farmers. This online platform facilitates the capture of information about the piggeries and the affected numbers, its scrutiny and verification by the respective District Veterinary Officer, approval of the eligible list of beneficiaries by the respective District Collector, processing and transfer of benefits. Relevant dashboards at various levels are provided that aids in effective monitoring and decision making. ','Product',NULL,'A','Others',14),(103,'e-Mart','','This is an online platform and mobile app for consumers to place orders from a wide range of local businesses/ farmers/manufactures etc. Anyone can register and add their products/ produce and reach out to potential consumers using this platform. This will significantly bridge the gap of supply and demand between the marginal businesses and the consumers. The process can be monitored and coordinated by the District Offices to ensure authenticity and reliability. ','Product',NULL,'A','Others',15),(104,'Nipuna','','It is a digital platform which can provide options of up-skilling workers or unemployed youth and thereafter helping them with appropriate placements. Once implemented, it can help equip the workers to enrich their skills and provide them with an increased chance of employability in and around their localities. It helps in unique worker identification, updated skill database, enhanced opportunities for employment etc.','Product',NULL,'A','Others',16),(105,'Panacea','Solution for Clinical Trials Registry','It is a platform to register the clinical trials conducted by various agencies across the globe. The objective is to ensure that a complete view of research is accessible to all those involved in health care decision making. This will improve research transparency and will ultimately strengthen the validity and value of the scientific evidence base. The registry would act as a primary register responsible in building up the database of all Clinical Trials in that country / region. ','Product',NULL,'A','Others',17),(106,'CHOICE FOR CHIEF ELECTORAL OFFICE, KERALA STATE','','The software solution CHOICE, was implemented in the 14 sub offices of the Office of Chief Electoral Officer in the state for creation, updation and maintenance of the electoral database in the state. The software maintains complete details of the elector including photograph, fingerprint and signature. Photo ID Cards are issued to the electors from the software. Through the search utility provided it is possible to filter names that appear in multiple locations thereby reducing the possibility of database tampering. The various functionalities automated by the software includes preparation of electoral roll, updations including additions, deletions & modifications, future revisions (summary, special, continuous & intensive), printing of rolls, preparation of CD ROMs of electoral rolls, preserving the database as archived copies and operation & management of electors photo identity card program.','Project','0.6066220840487614@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',105),(107,'FINANCIAL ACCOUNTING SOLUTION FOR KHADI & VILLAGE INDUSTRIES BOARD, GOVERNMENT OF KERALA','','A software solution was developed and deployed at the Finance Department of the Organization. The software consists of three major modules viz. Accounting Application, Loan Disbursement & Repayment, Khadi Information System. The accounts of the 405 Production units and 140 Shops are maintained in the software. The software facilitates the finalization of accounts including the generation of Balance Sheet, Profit & Loss Statement and various other mandatory statements. The Loan Disbursement & Repayment Module maintains details of the beneficiaries of the loan scheme and their repayments. The software also keeps track of the production and sales of Khadi products in the various units of the organization.','Project','0.6066220840487614@-@gok.jpg','A','Software Development',106);
